{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c58b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b2ff-60d1-7b92-bcfc-8a4c766633f3"},"sequence":288,"recorded_at":1780531400000571,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"b5be48e9-caa3-42a3-a29a-786d769c2b71","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"b5be48e9-caa3-42a3-a29a-786d769c2b71","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"b5be48e9-caa3-42a3-a29a-786d769c2b71"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b300-5efd-7b63-8bed-41ae09841bda"},"task_id":"01a0b300-5efd-7b63-8bed-41ae09841bda","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b300-5efd-7b63-8bed-41ae09841bda","chunk":"Read text file `/tmp/kkh1an-rev3/verdict.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-kkh1an — independent review verdict, CR-TASK-260830-kkh1an-3 revision 3\n2|\n3|**Verdict: CHANGES REQUESTED (routed `to-dev`).** No P1. One P2 production\n4|finding (F3: `ObserveFencing` never fences a stale incarnation whose\n5|observation carries no live fencing grant — the lapsed-grant and the\n6|no-grant/controller-restart members of the cold force takeover, under a local\n7|and a remote winner alike; `repeat-of: rev2 F2` class), one P2 evidence finding\n8|(E3: the per-effect authorization recheck is pinned on the lease-tuple axis\n9|only; an authorization that EXPIRES between effects commits the remaining\n10|effects under a one-line mutant with the whole suite green; `repeat-of: rev2 E2`\n11|class), and five P3 items. Everything else holds on the exact tree and is\n12|confirmed by my own instruments: F1 (same-key retry after `status`) meets the\n13|behavioural bar at the producer's seam and at my own engine seam with real\n14|SIGKILLs, F2's remote-winner arms fence and compose the landed gate, E1's\n15|create-row gates and E2's third-position rechecks and session axis are pinned\n16|and their mutants die, the shipped harness reproduces 100/100 twice, the ratio\n17|re-derives to 84 of 84, the full configured suite is green, hygiene is clean.\n18|\n19|Reviewer: RUN-260918-f6b44c (claude-opus-5 max). Reviewed bytes: base\n20|`c61fc06ad8190a73c3005e137282829936dac970` (the predecessor checkpoint = the\n21|Story branch tip), candidate tree `94dc630b5e2eb6c49e13e4b0beff7ee4b434493f`\n22|(recomputed from the live Story worktree with a temporary untracked-aware\n23|index: equal), patch sha256\n24|`ccac72639080b50614afc55463b6d4b68dcdab2b47055e38cf92364163557ba1` (equal to\n25|the CR record). Every probe ran in isolated `git archive` copies of the exact\n26|tree under `.temp/TASK-260830-kkh1an/review-rev3/` (`cand/` tree-exact checks,\n27|`cand-h/` shipped harness, `cand-m/` reviewer mutants, `cand-p/` probes; the\n28|copies' index trees equal the candidate OID before and after every run, and\n29|`cand-m`/`cand-p` differ from the candidate only by the two reviewer probe\n30|files). The live Story worktree, index, branch and HEAD were never touched\n31|(`git status` after the review is unchanged: `M LOGBOOK.md`, `M README.md`,\n32|`M internal/axpane/decide.go`, `M internal/terminalbackend/…` ×4,\n33|`?? internal/terminstance/`). `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1` everywhere, 0\n34|`__pycache__` in any copy. Every instrument, raw log and subprocess exit is in\n35|`TASK-260830-kkh1an_review-evidence-rev3.tar.gz` (paths below are relative to\n36|that archive).\n37|\n38|## 0. Rework verification (rev2 findings), graded on my own executed evidence\n39|\n40|| Rev2 finding | What I executed | Grade |\n41|| --- | --- | --- |\n42|| **F1** key poisoned forever; \"status, then same-key retry\" unimplementable | Producer real-kill tests `TestExecuteCrashChildSelfTerminates` / `TestExecuteCrashCreateResumesAfterStatus` PASS ×2 (`logs/60-realkill-run{1,2}.log`). My own real SIGKILL at the ENGINE `BeforeEffect` seam of `create` (`probes/zz_review3_crash_unix_test.go`, `TestRV3_RealKillBeforeFirstCreateEffectThenResume`, PASS ×2): child killed by SIGKILL, receipt durable, no completion, no effect ran → same-key retry with the backend read failing refuses `terminal_backend_unavailable` / `unavailable` / `status_first` with no effect → status proves absence (canonical non-match form) → same-key retry completes `active`/`replay_same` with exactly one instance's `[binding_persisted wrapper_started]`, one completion, exactly one exported receipt → a further identical retry replays the one result with no new effect. `TestRV3_IdempotencyReplayAndMismatchThroughEngine`: identical retry replays byte-equal; changed operation ID in-window is `idempotency_mismatch` / `idempotency key conflict` / source restored / `status_first`. | **Closed.** Behavioural bar met at two seams. |\n43|| **F2** stale incarnation under a remote winner never fenced | Committed `TestObserveFencingRemoteWinner{StaleEpoch,LosingLease}Fences` drive both remote members from `active`, `parked`, `quiescing`; `…WinningTokenLeavesState` pins the no-transition member. `TestRV3_RemoteWinnerLeaseSummaryHostIsTheOnlySwitch`: the direct question parks `remote_owner`, the relative question (only `LocalHostID` switched to `Winner.HolderHostID`, nothing fabricated) parks `stale_owner` with the winning lease `f47ac10b-…`. `TestRV3_FencingNoLocalTupleComparison`: `fencing.go` code lines reference no `presented.Epoch/LeaseID`, `Winner.Epoch/LeaseID`, `Grant.Token`; exactly two `fencing.Authorize(` calls. Shipped rows `N-fencing-remote`, `N-fencing-operation-remote`, `N-fencing-remote-stale-only` KILLED ×2; my `RV3-M6` (remote path skips the live-source gate) KILLED ×4 by the committed suite. | **Closed for the fresh-grant members; the grant-less members of the same class are open — F3 below.** |\n44|| **E1** create-row gates positive-path only at the engine | Shipped rows `N-engine-auth-entry` / `N-engine-generation-entry` are now the create-exempting mutants (`&& operation != terminalbackend.OperationCreate`) keyed to `TestExecuteCreateEntryAuthorizationRefuses` / `…GenerationRefuses`: KILLED ×2 with the receipt witness on the control-kind and foreign-lease members (`logs/mutants-pass1/N-engine-auth-entry.log`: \"Lookup(key) found a receipt for the unauthorized create, want none bound\") and the literal-token witness on the expired member; `N-engine-headless-absent` and `N-engine-committed-timeout-disposition` KILLED ×2. | **Closed.** (One note: the `expired` member kills on the code literal, not on the receipt — see E3.) |\n45|| **E2** recheck pinned at one position; session never compared | `N-engine-recheck-{auth,generation}-third` KILLED ×2 (rotation at the fourth `CurrentLease`/`CurrentGeneration` read, two effects committed); `N-status-session-{scoped,exact}` KILLED ×2; `N-status-match-*` ×5 KILLED ×2. | **Closed** for the tuple and generation axes; the expiry axis is E3. |\n46|| P3-1 pre-link store failure | `TestExecutePreLinkStoreFailureRestoresSource` (read-only pending dir → `after=active`, `required_operator_action`, no receipt); `N-engine-bind-{prelink,postlink}` KILLED ×2 | Closed |\n47|| P3-2 fencing sources | `fenceLive`: creating/parked/active/quiescing fence; absent/stopped/stale_fenced/unavailable surface the park; `N-fencing-source-{absent,stopped,creating}` KILLED ×2 | Closed |\n48|| P3-3 deadline instant | `TestExecuteEntryDeadlineInstantRefuses` (4 rows, no receipt) / `TestExecuteStatusDeadlineInstantRefuses` (no observation); rows KILLED ×2 | Closed |\n49|| P3-4 `attach`/`none` kind negatives | `N-auth-kind-{attach,none}` KILLED ×2 | Closed (the class recurs on another enum — P3-4 below) |\n50|| P3-5 match conjunction per axis | `TestExecuteStatusIdentityMatchEachAxis` 10 subtests; 5 rows KILLED ×2 | Closed |\n51|| P3-6 `kindFor` twin | landed `terminalbackend.TransitionAuthorization` accessor + column test + census/inventory/audit registration; `TestKindForAgreesWithLandedTable`; `N-engine-kind-map` re-keyed KILLED ×2; the three terminalbackend pins PASS (`logs/82`) | Closed |\n52|| P3-7 `unavailable`+`new_authorization` | kept as the leaf's stated mapping contract, recorded as a literal tension in TRACEABILITY | Acceptable (stated) |\n53|| `holder_host_id` unbound | stated in `CheckAuthorization` doc + TRACEABILITY | Acceptable (stated) |\n54|| TRACEABILITY 70/71 + \"recovers through status\" prose | reworded to the resumed behaviour; LOGBOOK carries an explicit REVERSAL entry | Closed |\n55|\n56|## 1. What holds (verified myself on the exact tree)\n57|\n58|| Check | Result | Evidence |\n59|| --- | --- | --- |\n60|| gofmt / go vet / go build; GOOS=linux and GOOS=windows builds; GOOS=windows vet of the package | all exit 0 | `logs/02` |\n61|| `go test ./internal/terminstance -count=1 -v` | exit 0, 101 top-level `--- PASS` (224 incl. subtests), 0 FAIL, 0 SKIP | `logs/01` |\n62|| `go test ./... -count=1` on the exact tree, rerun by me | exit 0, 40/40 packages `ok` (4m34s) | `logs/04` |\n63|| `-race` on terminstance, terminalbackend, axpane, fencing; `-cover` terminstance 85.6%; `git diff --check` | all ok / exit 0 | `logs/70` |\n64|| tracecheck (registry untouched: contracts=64, clauses 56/569 — trunk figures) / `cataloggen -adopted … -check` | exit 0 / exit 0, tree unmodified | `logs/71` |\n65|| CR construction suite | runtime-recorded `required=30 green=30 failed=0 missing=0` on the exact tree (accepted from the attached `_rev3-validation.log`; the whole-repo race gate, the 17 fuzz gates, JSON validity and `task-board validate` were not rerun by me) | resource |\n66|| Shipped harness, isolated pristine copy, two full passes with raw per-plant output | 100/100 both passes (98 narrowing KILLED + 1 tightening KILLED + `C-control` SURVIVED), verdict lists identical, 100 raw logs per pass with subprocess exits, `cand-h` index tree equal to the candidate OID and working tree clean after each pass | `logs/40-harness-pass{1,2}-verdicts.log`, `logs/mutants-pass{1,2}/`, `logs/40-harness-driver.log` |\n67|| Real-kill evidence | producer's two seams PASS ×2; my engine `BeforeEffect` seam PASS ×2; my `AfterEffect`-of-`binding_persisted` seam characterized ×2 (below) | `logs/60` |\n68|| Ratio | 84 data rows counted in `TRACEABILITY.md` (numbered 1..84, unique); 95 distinct cited top-level tests, every one present in `go test -list` (94 in-package + the terminalbackend column test) and every one `--- PASS` in my verbose run; every explicitly cited subtest PASS; rows 53/54 are cross-references to driven rows. | `logs/82` |\n69|| Spec fidelity (§4.C extracted from `SPEC.v0.7.0.md` lines 1082–1218 and diffed): eight-state enum, ten operations, ten side effects, transition matrix, allowed-error sets, key shapes all landed (`terminalbackend`) and composed, never re-spelled; `AXAuthorization` closed 7-member set; epoch bound witnessed at 1, 9007199254740991, 0, 9007199254740992 at `ParseAXAuthorization` (committed) and through the nested `MutationContext` and the quiesce-input BODY (`TestRV3_EpochBoundThroughNestedSurfaces`); `RetryDisposition` closed 4 (copy-counting census + parse pin, literal tokens at `conformance_test.go:235`); `ProviderProofKind` closed 3; `AuthorizationKind` closed 4; key material asserted as whole literal strings (`TestRV3_KeyMaterialLiteral`: `…bbb1/quiesce/…ddd1`, `…/boundary/…/provider_process_exit`, `…/stop/sha256:bbb…`, `session/bootstrap`); an outside-set code on the first effect of each of the four rows is `terminal_backend_protocol_error` / `operation error vocabulary` and status's outside-set report the same, status timeout and uncoded read failure return an error with NO report (`TestRV3_OutsideSetCodeRefusedPerRow`) | holds | `logs/12` |\n70|| State-entry rules: `creating` only via create after the receipt (`InterimState` + `AfterReceipt`, real kill); pre-effect errors restore the source; post-effect unprovable → `unavailable`/`status_first`; only quiesce-input → `quiescing`; `stale_fenced` only via `ObserveFencing` (no `StateStaleFenced` in the engine); per-effect tuple+generation rechecks at positions 1, 2, 3; deadline never cancels a committed effect (`RV3-M7` KILLED ×4) | holds (with F3/E3 caveats) | source read, harness, `logs/50` |\n71|| Generation bound 0/256/257 (chars not bytes) on the context, the status body, the result and the Go twin with the landed `terminal_backend_stale_generation`; Binding object and CLI Result 4 stated as bounds (verified unchanged from rev2) | holds | committed tests, `logs/01` |\n72|| Composition: `fencing.Authorize`/`ParkDetails` (two composed questions), `terminalbackend.CheckTransition/CheckErrorAllowed/CheckOperation/CheckStatusResult/IdempotencyKey/GenerationDigest/CheckVersionTuple/ParseID/TransitionAuthorization`, `environ.DecodeStrictObject/Check*`, `scalar.Parse*` — no second enum, no local tuple comparison, no second JSON discipline | holds | source read, `TestRV3_FencingNoLocalTupleComparison` |\n73|| Bounds and hygiene: changed paths = exactly the 39 candidate paths; `internal/traceability` untouched; `task-board.config.json` equal to base and to trunk `c3aae73`; 0 `__pycache__`/`.pyc` in the tree; README +52/−0 with test/harness commands and the explicit no-`ax`/no-`doctor`/no-capability sentence; LOGBOOK +21/−0 newest-first with the rev2-F2 REVERSAL; `tmux`/`ConPTY`/`syscall`/`os/exec` in production only inside the two stated-bound comments; trunk→candidate touches only the Story's paths | holds | `logs/80` |\n74|| Producer evidence archive: task-scoped README, 253-entry `MANIFEST.sha256`, 100 raw per-plant logs on both passes, cmd01..cmd29 logs, `.go` sha listing equal before/after the race gate, 0 pycache, 0 foreign-task files | hygienic | `logs/81` |\n75|\n76|## 2. Coverage statement\n77|\n78|Producer claim: 84 of 84 rows driven. Re-derived: 84 data rows, every named\n79|test and subtest exists and passed (`logs/82`). **I measure 84 of 84 driven**\n80|at the named production entries. Three rows' prose outruns what the tests\n81|show: rows 46/47/77/78 (\"stale_fenced only via fencing observation … non-stale\n82|observations leave state\") are driven on fresh-grant observations only — the\n83|lapsed-grant and no-grant members of the stale class are not fenced (F3); row\n84|48 (\"auth rechecked before each effect\") is driven on the lease-tuple axis\n85|only (E3); row 40 (\"shape arms … evidence\") is driven without the `[0..256]`\n86|edge (P3-1).\n87|\n88|## 3. Findings\n89|\n90|No P1: the eight-state enum, the operation/effect vocabularies and the\n91|transition matrix are the landed ones; no second state machine, no second\n92|fencing model.\n93|\n94|### P2 — production\n95|\n96|- **F3 (P2, `repeat-of: rev2 F2` class — a member of the stale-incarnation\n97|  class that `ObserveFencing` does not fence). A stale incarnation whose\n98|  observation carries no LIVE fencing grant is never fenced.** `fencing.go:59`\n99|  asks the landed `Authorize` first as the local host and, on `remote_owner`,\n100|  again from the winner's host; both questions run inside the landed gate,\n101|  whose arm order (`gate.go:295–375`) evaluates `HasGrant` (\"carries no grant;\n102|  validate the winning token first\", `ErrInvalidArguments`) and grant expiry\n103|  (\"lapsed; revalidate\", `ErrLeaseConflict`) BEFORE the direction and tuple\n104|  arms. Neither is a park, so `ObserveFencing` returns `(current, false, err)`\n105|  and the incarnation stays `active`/`parked`/`quiescing`. Witnesses\n106|  (`probes/zz_review3_probe_test.go`, `logs/13`):\n107|  `TestRV3_NoGrantHidesStaleness` — `HasGrant=false`, `Verified=true`,\n108|  well-formed epoch-2 winner, presented epoch-1 token, from `active`, `parked`\n109|  and `quiescing`, under a local AND a remote winner: six times \"no\n110|  transition\"; `TestRV3_LapsedGrantHidesStaleness` — the same with a grant\n111|  validated 2h ago under a 1h refresh interval: \"lapsed; revalidate the winning\n112|  token\", no transition, local and remote. This is not \"refresh first\": a stale\n113|  owner can never obtain a fresh grant, because `sessrepo.VerifyFencingToken`\n114|  (`lease_store.go:427–465`) refuses a token below the winning epoch\n115|  (`ErrStaleLeaseEpoch`) and a token from another holder\n116|  (`ErrLeaseHolderMismatch`), and grants are \"machine-local transient state:\n117|  never persisted\" (`lease_store.go:163–171`), so after a controller restart\n118|  the prior owner has none. These are exactly the cold force-takeover members\n119|  §13.7 exists for (B force-takes because A is silent longer than the refresh\n120|  interval; \"the prior owner becomes stale\", \"the loser MUST stop accepting\n121|  input when it learns the winner\"): input IS blocked by the landed input gate\n122|  (fail-closed, same arm), but the Terminal Instance projection never reaches\n123|  `stale_fenced`, so the `terminate-stale` row (`stale_fenced|unavailable →\n124|  stopped`, final leaf) cannot target the incarnation from that state — the\n125|  same consequence rev2 F2 was graded on. The only fenced members are the\n126|  \"hot\" ones (A still holding a grant younger than the refresh interval when\n127|  it observes the takeover). The doc comment (\"any non-stale refusal or park\n128|  (unverified, ambiguous, no winner) surfaces its own error with no\n129|  transition, because only proven staleness fences\"), README (\"`stale_fenced`\n130|  is entered only by fencing observation … including under a remote winner\")\n131|  and TRACEABILITY rows 47/77 name neither member; the observation itself\n132|  proves staleness (verified winner, well-formed, older epoch) and the\n133|  projection says \"not stale\". Note for fairness: rev2's rework scope offered\n134|  this composition as its first option and it carries this blind spot; the\n135|  finding is new, not a rework miss. Fix without forking: land an exported\n136|  staleness verdict in `internal/fencing` over a verified, well-formed winner\n137|  (the direction/tuple arms only, no grant precondition — the grant governs\n138|  AUTHORIZATION, not the fact of staleness) and compose it for the projection;\n139|  or, if the product decision is that fencing observation is grant-gated,\n140|  state that bound explicitly in `doc.go`/TRACEABILITY/README and name the\n141|  route the final leaf must supply for the lapsed/no-grant members. Either way\n142|  drive both members from `active`/`parked`/`quiescing` under local and remote\n143|  winners with a narrowing row per arm.\n144|\n145|### P2 — evidence\n146|\n147|- **E3 (P2, `repeat-of: rev2 E2` class — the per-effect recheck not closed).\n148|  The per-effect authorization recheck is pinned on the lease-tuple axis only;\n149|  the EXPIRY axis is unmeasured at every position.** Reviewer mutant `RV3-M1`\n150|  (`probes/review3_mutants.py`, `logs/50-rv3-mutants-pass{1..4}.log`,\n151|  raw logs and diffs in `logs/rv3-mutants-pass{1..4}/`): `runEffects` reads\n152|  `entryNow := engine.Now()` once before the loop and passes it to every\n153|  in-loop `CheckAuthorization` (the lease tuple is still re-read per effect)\n154|  — **SURVIVED ×4** against the committed suite, while the witness\n155|  `TestRV3W_M1_AuthExpiryRecheckedBeforeEachEffect` passes pristine and fails\n156|  under the mutant ×4: a request-stop whose authorization expires after the\n157|  first effect (deadline 2026-09-03 > expiry 2026-09-02, `Now` advanced past\n158|  the expiry after effect 1) commits `process_closed` and `backend_store_closed`\n159|  under an expired authorization and reports `stopped`/`replay_same`;\n160|  pristine refuses `terminal_backend_unauthorized` / `ax authorization expiry`\n161|  before the second effect with `after=unavailable`, `new_authorization`,\n162|  exactly one committed effect. Root cause in the fixture: `fixtureExpires`\n163|  (2026-09-02T00:00Z) lies AFTER `fixtureDeadline` (2026-09-01T18:00Z), so no\n164|  committed test can observe the expiry arm independently of the deadline arm\n165|  at any position (the same confound makes the E1 `expired` subtest kill on\n166|  the code literal rather than on the receipt: under a create-exempting mutant\n167|  the deadline gate refuses `terminal_backend_timeout` and binds nothing). The\n168|  shipped rows `N-engine-recheck-auth{,-third}` weaken the whole\n169|  `CheckAuthorization` call and are killed by the tuple rotation; a mutant\n170|  that keeps the tuple and drops the expiry walks through. DoD: \"negative\n171|  tests that fail when the gate admits what it must reject\" is not met for\n172|  the expiry member of the per-effect gate (\"an expiring AX authorization\";\n173|  \"rechecked immediately before each side effect\"). The witness above is\n174|  committable as is; add a harness row for it.\n175|\n176|### P3\n177|\n178|- **P3-1 Evidence bound edge unwitnessed.** `RV3-M2` (`checkSortedUniqueEvidenceWhere`\n179|  `> 256` → `> 257`) SURVIVED ×4; witness `TestRV3W_M2_EvidenceBoundEdge`\n180|  (256 admitted / 257 refused on `CheckResult` — `result evidence bound` — and\n181|  on `ExecuteStatus` — `status evidence bound`) fails under it ×4. No committed\n182|  test carries more than a handful of evidence IDs. Adjacent-edge class.\n183|- **P3-2 The capability-conditional refusal arm's disposition is unpinned at\n184|  the engine.** `RV3-M3` (`execute.go:257–260`: `DispositionFor(code,false)` →\n185|  `DispositionStatusFirst`) SURVIVED ×4; `TestRV3W_M3_ConditionalCapabilityDisposition`\n186|  (headless create from `stopped`, wait without `safe_boundary_observation`,\n187|  provider kind without `provider_process_observation` → literal\n188|  `required_operator_action`) fails under it ×4. `TestDispositionForMapping`\n189|  pins the helper; the committed engine tests for this arm assert code, detail\n190|  and `after` but never the disposition (`create_gates_test.go:92–93`,\n191|  `lifecycle_test.go:45,73`). Rule pinned at the helper, not at this entry.\n192|- **P3-3 Status report `last_operation_id` grammar unwitnessed.** `RV3-M8`\n193|  (`execute.go:540`: admit exactly the empty string) SURVIVED ×4;\n194|  `TestRV3W_M8_StatusLastOperationGrammar` (`\"\"`, `nope`, upper-case UUID →\n195|  `status report operation`) fails under it ×4. `TestExecuteStatusReportMemberRefusals`\n196|  drifts session/backend/versions/instance/generation but never the last\n197|  operation ID; the arm exists (`execute.go:540–543`) with no negative.\n198|- **P3-4 `ParseProviderProofKind` admits a landed sibling name under a\n199|  narrowing (same class as rev2 P3-4).** `RV3-M4` (default arm admits the\n200|  capability name `provider_process_observation` as `provider_quiescence`)\n201|  SURVIVED ×4; `TestRV3W_M4_ProofKindSiblingNamesRefused` (the two capability\n202|  names, the side-effect name `safe_boundary_observed`, `provider_exit`,\n203|  upper-case and trailing-space spellings, at the direct entry and through\n204|  the wait body) fails under it ×4. The AST census counts case clauses only;\n205|  the committed corpus (`provider_restart`, …) has no landed sibling names.\n206|  Extend the corpus (and the `RetryDisposition`/`AuthorizationKind` corpora\n207|  with their sibling vocabularies the same way).\n208|- **P3-5 The partial-progress member of the create recovery is unstated.**\n209|  `TestRV3_PartialCreateProgressIsNotResumable` and my real kill at the\n210|  `AfterEffect` seam of `binding_persisted` (`TestRV3_RealKillAfterFirstCreateEffect`,\n211|  ×2): receipt durable, one effect committed, no completion; a backend that\n212|  reports the interim `creating` with identity match → the same-key retry\n213|  refuses `terminal_backend_unavailable` / `unavailable` / `status_first`\n214|  and the key stays parked (the only exit is `unavailable → terminate-stale`,\n215|  final leaf); a backend that reports the instance `absent` (binding without\n216|  wrapper) → the retry resumes and re-performs BOTH effects under the same\n217|  receipt, one completion, one receipt. Both are defensible under \"Only a\n218|  successful status read proves absence\" and the backend's key binding, but\n219|  TRACEABILITY's bound names only \"the proven TARGET (or closed)\"; name the\n220|  interim-proven member and its exit route.\n221|\n222|### Characterizations (not findings)\n223|\n224|- After a successful status read proves the TARGET (`quiescing`), the same-key\n225|  quiesce retry refuses `terminal_backend_unavailable` with\n226|  `after=unavailable` / `status_first` (`TestRV3_TargetProvenRetryProjectsUnavailable`):\n227|  the local observation regresses from the just-proven target to\n228|  `unavailable`. §4.C's \"an error after an effect whose result cannot be\n229|  proven moves the local observation to unavailable with status_first\"\n230|  supports the mapping (the lost result's evidence is unprovable); recorded\n231|  because the caller has just been told `quiescing` by the same engine.\n232|- Wait-safe-boundary resumption re-performs `safe_boundary_observed` and\n233|  records the proof the backend returns now (`TestRV3_WaitResumptionReissuesBoundary`);\n234|  \"identical retry returns the same proof\" is delegated to the backend's key\n235|  binding — stated as a bound in TRACEABILITY, accepted.\n236|- `RV3-M6` (remote path fences any source) and `RV3-M7` (in-loop deadline\n237|  skipped once committed) are KILLED ×4 by the committed suite: the live-source\n238|  gate and \"a deadline cancels waiting, not a committed effect\" are pinned.\n239|\n240|## 4. DoD walk (live merged checklist)\n241|\n242|Production entry points implement the scoped deliverable — the rows, gates,\n243|receipts, rechecks, resumption and remote-winner fencing exist; the grant-less\n244|members of the stale class are not fenced (F3). Positive/negative/recovery\n245|tests pass with logs — yes for what is committed. README/traceability without\n246|unsupported claims — README's \"including under a remote winner\" and\n247|TRACEABILITY rows 47/77 outrun the code for the grant-less members (F3).\n248|Uncommitted in the Story worktree — yes (tree OID equal). Ratio — 84 of 84\n249|with call sites. Negative tests that fail when the gate admits — not for the\n250|expiry member of the per-effect recheck (E3). Narrowing mutant per gate —\n251|shipped 99 KILLED ×2 with a working control; five reviewer narrowings SURVIVED\n252|×4 with non-equivalent witnesses (E3, P3-1..P3-4). No source-text gate in\n253|production (the AST census is a test instrument; its blind spot is P3-4).\n254|Lint/build — clean. Outcome artifacts — attached and hygienic. Logbook —\n255|newest-first, additive, with the explicit reversal. Implementation matches AC —\n256|not for the cold-takeover fencing members (F3). Fits the architecture — yes\n257|(composition over the landed owners; the fix for F3 belongs in\n258|`internal/fencing` as an exported verdict, not in a local comparison). Tests\n259|green — yes. Gates attacked, not read — yes, and the attack found the gaps\n260|above.\n261|\n262|## 5. Instruments (all in the evidence archive)\n263|\n264|`probes/zz_review3_probe_test.go` (16 top-level probes: 5 witnesses `TestRV3W_M{1,2,3,4,8}_*`,\n265|5 CHARACTERIZATION probes, 6 direct re-verifications; all 16 PASS pristine,\n266|`logs/12`, `logs/13`), `probes/zz_review3_crash_unix_test.go` (2 real-kill\n267|probes, PASS ×2 each, `logs/60`), `probes/review3_mutants.py` (7 narrowing\n268|rows + 3 controls; committed-suite and witness runs; 4 passes with identical\n269|verdicts: M1/M2/M3/M4/M8 SURVIVED with witness KILLED, M6/M7 KILLED, `RV3-K`\n270|known-kill KILLED, `RV3-C` comment control SURVIVED, `RV3-B` build-break\n271|control reported `ERROR(build broke)`; raw per-plant logs with exits and\n272|diffs in `logs/rv3-mutants-pass{1..4}/`; the working tree of `cand-m` differs\n273|from the candidate index by nothing after every pass), `probes/run_harness.sh`\n274|+ `probes/split_raw.py` (shipped harness driver: `logs/40-*`,\n275|`logs/mutants-pass{1,2}/` 100 raw logs each), `logs/01`, `02`, `04`, `70`,\n276|`71`, `80`, `81`, `82`, `REVIEW-MANIFEST.txt` (sha256 of every file).\n277|\n278|## Rework scope (for the producer)\n279|\n280|1. **F3 — fence the grant-less members of the stale class** (P2,\n281|   `repeat-of: rev2 F2` class). Land an exported staleness verdict in\n282|   `internal/fencing` that decides the direction/tuple arms over a verified,\n283|   well-formed winner WITHOUT the grant precondition (the grant authorizes; it\n284|   does not make an incarnation less stale), compose it for `ObserveFencing`'s\n285|   second question (or for both questions), and drive the no-grant and the\n286|   lapsed-grant members from `active`/`parked`/`quiescing` under a local and a\n287|   remote winner, keeping unverified/ambiguous/no-winner as no-transition.\n288|   Ship a narrowing row per new arm and the named regression test the\n289|   `repeat-of` rule asks for. If instead the product decision is that fencing\n290|   observation is grant-gated, say so explicitly in `doc.go`, TRACEABILITY and\n291|   the README sentence, and name the recovery route the final leaf owes for\n292|   these members — silence is the finding.\n293|2. **E3 — pin the expiry axis of the per-effect recheck** (P2 evidence,\n294|   `repeat-of: rev2 E2` class): commit `TestRV3W_M1_AuthExpiryRecheckedBeforeEachEffect`\n295|   or its equivalent (a context whose deadline lies after the authorization\n296|   expiry; `Now` advanced past the expiry after effect 1; literal\n297|   `ax authorization expiry`, `after=unavailable`, `new_authorization`, one\n298|   committed effect) and a harness row that keeps the tuple recheck and drops\n299|   the expiry recheck. Consider a second fixture instant between the deadline\n300|   and the expiry so the E1 `expired` member also kills on the receipt.\n301|3. P3-1..P3-4: commit the four witnesses (`TestRV3W_M2/M3/M4/M8_*` are\n302|   committable as is) with harness rows; P3-5: state the interim-proven\n303|   member of the create recovery and its exit route. Keep everything else as\n304|   is — the rest of the revision holds and my instruments confirm it.\n305|\n306|Verdict recorded by RUN-260918-f6b44c; no product edits, commits, checkpoints\n307|or integration were performed; the isolated copies are deleted after\n308|attachment. `commit_ack` is not supplied.","final_result":true}}}
