{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c693","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b2ff-60d1-7b92-bcfc-8a4c766633f3"},"sequence":420,"recorded_at":1780531400000835,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"b5be48e9-caa3-42a3-a29a-786d769c2b71","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"b5be48e9-caa3-42a3-a29a-786d769c2b71","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"b5be48e9-caa3-42a3-a29a-786d769c2b71"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b300-9f94-7850-bfb9-f7268c0529a3"},"task_id":"01a0b300-9f94-7850-bfb9-f7268c0529a3","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b300-9f94-7850-bfb9-f7268c0529a3","chunk":"Read text file `internal/terminstance/fencing.go`.\n1|package terminstance\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/fencing\"\n5|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/terminalbackend\"\n6|)\n7|\n8|// ObserveFencing projects one AX fencing observation onto the Terminal\n9|// Instance lifecycle. It is the ONLY entry that produces stale_fenced:\n10|// no backend operation targets that state (the landed CheckTransition\n11|// proves it and the engine never synthesizes it), only AX fencing\n12|// observation does.\n13|//\n14|// The verdict is read entirely from the landed fencing projection: the\n15|// presented local token is authorized against the observation through\n16|// fencing.Authorize with the restore operation, and a ParkStaleOwner\n17|// park — the older-epoch arm and the same-epoch lease-mismatch arm\n18|// alike — moves the local observation to stale_fenced. The operation\n19|// must be launch-class (restore or activation): the input, mutation\n20|// and checkpoint entries refuse a stale token instead of parking it,\n21|// which would surface as an error and never fence. Restore is chosen\n22|// over activation because it gates terminal restore, this story's\n23|// domain; the two are equivalent on the stale arms.\n24|//\n25|// A stale token under a REMOTE winner fences too: the landed gate parks\n26|// remote_owner before it compares tuples (\"the operative fact beats the\n27|// credential\"), so the first verdict cannot distinguish a stale token\n28|// from the winning token under a foreign winner. The second question\n29|// asks the landed gate whether the presented token is stale RELATIVE TO\n30|// THE WINNER by authorizing from the winner's own host (LocalHostID set\n31|// to Winner.HolderHostID) and reading the park: stale_owner fences,\n32|// anything else — including the winning token authorizing cleanly —\n33|// leaves the state with the original remote park. Both questions run\n34|// inside the landed Authorize; no local tuple comparison exists here.\n35|//\n36|// Only a live incarnation fences: creating, parked, active and\n37|// quiescing move to stale_fenced, while absent and stopped (no\n38|// incarnation exists for terminate-stale to target), stale_fenced\n39|// itself (already fenced: the transition is idempotent) and\n40|// unavailable (the observation is unknown and no verdict is projected\n41|// over unknown) surface the park with no transition. Every other\n42|// outcome leaves the state untouched: an authorized token reports no\n43|// transition, and any non-stale refusal or park (unverified, ambiguous,\n44|// no winner) surfaces its own error with no transition, because only\n45|// proven staleness fences. A nil error with transitioned false is the\n46|// authorized case.\n47|//\n48|// This function performs no lease comparison of its own: the tuple,\n49|// grant, expiry and direction arms all run inside the landed Authorize,\n50|// so no second fencing model exists here. It reads Winner.LeaseID and\n51|// Winner.Epoch only through Authorize's verdict, never Winner.Checkpoint:\n52|// lease records are immutable content-addressed blobs whose checkpoint\n53|// member is null for every epoch-1 lease, so keying on it would be\n54|// vacuous for every session that never changed hands.\n55|func ObserveFencing(current terminalbackend.InstanceState, presented fencing.PresentedToken, observation fencing.Observation) (terminalbackend.InstanceState, bool, error) {\n56|\tif _, err := terminalbackend.ParseInstanceState(string(current)); err != nil {\n57|\t\treturn current, false, wrapLanded(err)\n58|\t}\n59|\t_, authErr := fencing.Authorize(fencing.OperationRestore, presented, observation)\n60|\tif authErr == nil {\n61|\t\treturn current, false, nil\n62|\t}\n63|\treason, _, parked := fencing.ParkDetails(authErr)\n64|\tif parked && reason == fencing.ParkRemoteOwner {\n65|\t\treturn observeRemoteWinner(current, presented, observation, authErr)\n66|\t}\n67|\tif parked && reason == fencing.ParkStaleOwner {\n68|\t\treturn fenceLive(current, authErr)\n69|\t}\n70|\treturn current, false, authErr\n71|}\n72|\n73|// observeRemoteWinner resolves a remote-winner park: the winner is on\n74|// another host and the presented token may be stale relative to it (the\n75|// force-takeover case) or the winning token itself observed from afar.\n76|// The landed gate decides from the winner's own host; only a stale\n77|// verdict fences, and only from a live incarnation.\n78|func observeRemoteWinner(current terminalbackend.InstanceState, presented fencing.PresentedToken, observation fencing.Observation, authErr error) (terminalbackend.InstanceState, bool, error) {\n79|\trelative := observation\n80|\trelative.LocalHostID = observation.Winner.HolderHostID\n81|\t_, relativeErr := fencing.Authorize(fencing.OperationRestore, presented, relative)\n82|\tif relativeErr == nil {\n83|\t\treturn current, false, authErr\n84|\t}\n85|\tif relativeReason, _, relativeParked := fencing.ParkDetails(relativeErr); relativeParked && relativeReason == fencing.ParkStaleOwner {\n86|\t\treturn fenceLive(current, authErr)\n87|\t}\n88|\treturn current, false, authErr\n89|}\n90|\n91|// fenceLive moves a live incarnation to stale_fenced and leaves every\n92|// other source untouched with the park that proved staleness. Absent\n93|// and stopped name no incarnation, stale_fenced is already fenced, and\n94|// unavailable is unknown: none of them transitions.\n95|func fenceLive(current terminalbackend.InstanceState, authErr error) (terminalbackend.InstanceState, bool, error) {\n96|\tswitch current {\n97|\tcase terminalbackend.StateCreating, terminalbackend.StateParked,\n98|\t\tterminalbackend.StateActive, terminalbackend.StateQuiescing:\n99|\t\treturn terminalbackend.StateStaleFenced, true, nil\n100|\tdefault:\n101|\t\treturn current, false, authErr\n102|\t}\n103|}","final_result":true}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c695","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b2ff-60d1-7b92-bcfc-8a4c766633f3"},"sequence":421,"recorded_at":1780531400000837,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"b5be48e9-caa3-42a3-a29a-786d769c2b71","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"b5be48e9-caa3-42a3-a29a-786d769c2b71","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"b5be48e9-caa3-42a3-a29a-786d769c2b71"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b300-9f94-7850-bfb9-f7268c0529a3"},"task_id":"01a0b300-9f94-7850-bfb9-f7268c0529a3","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"01a0b300-9f94-7850-bfb9-f7268c0529a3"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c697","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b2ff-60d1-7b92-bcfc-8a4c766633f3"},"sequence":422,"recorded_at":1780531400000839,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"b5be48e9-caa3-42a3-a29a-786d769c2b71","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"b5be48e9-caa3-42a3-a29a-786d769c2b71","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"b5be48e9-caa3-42a3-a29a-786d769c2b71"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b300-9fdf-7aa2-b6f9-ec316583640c"},"task_id":"01a0b300-9fdf-7aa2-b6f9-ec316583640c","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b300-9fdf-7aa2-b6f9-ec316583640c","chunk":"Read text file `internal/fencing/gate.go`.\n1|package fencing\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"errors\"\n5|\t\"fmt\"\n6|\t\"time\"\n7|\n8|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/scalar\"\n9|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/sessrepo\"\n10|)\n11|\n12|var (\n13|\t// ErrLeaseConflict is the Section 15 lease_conflict refusal at exit\n14|\t// 10: the presented fencing proof is not the winning authority for\n15|\t// this session (same-epoch loser, epoch beyond the winner, foreign\n16|\t// session, lapsed grant, or absent/ambiguous/unverified ownership on\n17|\t// a non-launch entry), or a forged capability reached a consumer.\n18|\tErrLeaseConflict = errors.New(\"lease_conflict\")\n19|\t// ErrNotOwner is the Section 15 not_owner refusal at exit 10: the\n20|\t// winning lease holder is a remote host and this entry is not a\n21|\t// launch, so there is no parked direction to take.\n22|\tErrNotOwner = errors.New(\"not_owner\")\n23|\t// ErrStaleOwner is the Section 15 stale_owner refusal at exit 10:\n24|\t// the presented epoch precedes the winning epoch on a non-launch\n25|\t// entry. Launch entries park with the stale_owner reason instead.\n26|\tErrStaleOwner = errors.New(\"stale_owner\")\n27|\t// ErrParked marks a park decision: the launch is refused and the\n28|\t// session must park carrying the session.parked reason and winning\n29|\t// lease ID. It always wraps the underlying Section 15 cause as\n30|\t// well, so errors.Is reports both the decision and the class.\n31|\tErrParked = errors.New(\"parked\")\n32|\t// ErrInvalidArguments is the Section 15 invalid_arguments refusal\n33|\t// at exit 2: the gate call itself is malformed (unknown operation,\n34|\t// malformed presented token or winning summary, missing grant,\n35|\t// missing clock reading, unusable policy, or unknown provider\n36|\t// operation). The caller fixes the call, not the ownership.\n37|\tErrInvalidArguments = errors.New(\"invalid_arguments\")\n38|\t// ErrLocalPreconditionFailed is the Section 15\n39|\t// local_precondition_failed refusal at exit 3, the class the\n40|\t// Section 4.C terminate-stale row names: terminate-stale without\n41|\t// explicit force recovery, without preserved diagnostics, without\n42|\t// an established winner, or against the live winning owner.\n43|\tErrLocalPreconditionFailed = errors.New(\"local_precondition_failed\")\n44|)\n45|\n46|// refuse is the single refusal funnel every fencing rejection flows\n47|// through. No production path wraps a sentinel with fmt.Errorf directly.\n48|var refuse = func(sentinel error, format string, arguments ...any) error {\n49|\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"%w: %s\", sentinel, fmt.Sprintf(format, arguments...))\n50|}\n51|\n52|// ParkReason is one Section 5.2 session.parked reason: the exact\n53|// vocabulary a park decision carries.\n54|type ParkReason string\n55|\n56|const (\n57|\t// ParkRemoteOwner parks because the winning lease holder is remote.\n58|\tParkRemoteOwner ParkReason = \"remote_owner\"\n59|\t// ParkStaleOwner parks because the local fencing proof loses to the\n60|\t// winning lease while the winner is local (a stale cache).\n61|\tParkStaleOwner ParkReason = \"stale_owner\"\n62|\t// ParkRestorePolicy parks because ownership cannot be verified:\n63|\t// no winning lease, unverified sync, ambiguous observations, or a\n64|\t// token from an epoch beyond the winner.\n65|\tParkRestorePolicy ParkReason = \"restore_policy\"\n66|\t// ParkFailedHandoff parks because the caller's handoff already\n67|\t// failed: a losing force lease must never activate.\n68|\tParkFailedHandoff ParkReason = \"failed_handoff\"\n69|)\n70|\n71|// parkRefusal carries a park decision: the session.parked reason, the\n72|// winning lease ID the parked event repeats (empty when no winner is\n73|// established), and the underlying Section 15 cause. It unwraps to both\n74|// ErrParked and the cause.\n75|type parkRefusal struct {\n76|\treason         ParkReason\n77|\twinningLeaseID string\n78|\tcause          error\n79|}\n80|\n81|func (refusal *parkRefusal) Error() string {\n82|\tif refusal.winningLeaseID == \"\" {\n83|\t\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"%s: park (%s); no winning lease is established\", ErrParked, refusal.reason)\n84|\t}\n85|\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"%s: park (%s) under winning lease %s: %v\", ErrParked, refusal.reason, refusal.winningLeaseID, refusal.cause)\n86|}\n87|\n88|func (refusal *parkRefusal) Unwrap() []error {\n89|\treturn []error{ErrParked, refusal.cause}\n90|}\n91|\n92|// IsParked reports whether err is a park decision rather than a hard\n93|// refusal. A parked launch must emit the session.parked vocabulary,\n94|// never start a runtime.\n95|func IsParked(err error) bool {\n96|\treturn errors.Is(err, ErrParked)\n97|}\n98|\n99|// ParkDetails extracts the session.parked vocabulary from a park\n100|// decision: the reason and the winning lease ID (empty when no winner\n101|// is established). It reports false for a hard refusal.\n102|func ParkDetails(err error) (ParkReason, string, bool) {\n103|\tvar parked *parkRefusal\n104|\tif !errors.As(err, &parked) {\n105|\t\treturn \"\", \"\", false\n106|\t}\n107|\treturn parked.reason, parked.winningLeaseID, true\n108|}\n109|\n110|// park builds the launch-class refusal for one ownership condition: the\n111|// parked reason with the Section 15 cause the same condition refuses\n112|// on a non-launch entry.\n113|func park(reason ParkReason, winningLeaseID string, cause error) error {\n114|\treturn &parkRefusal{reason: reason, winningLeaseID: winningLeaseID, cause: cause}\n115|}\n116|\n117|// Operation is one activation-class action the gate authorizes.\n118|type Operation string\n119|\n120|const (\n121|\t// OperationActivation gates provider activation and launch: only\n122|\t// the winning committed lease may create a destination runtime.\n123|\tOperationActivation Operation = \"activation\"\n124|\t// OperationInput gates provider input after attach (the\n125|\t// quiesce-input and attach direction): the owner revalidates\n126|\t// before accepting operator input.\n127|\tOperationInput Operation = \"input\"\n128|\t// OperationMutation gates owner-authored mutation: event append\n129|\t// and compare-and-swap succession carry the winning epoch.\n130|\tOperationMutation Operation = \"mutation\"\n131|\t// OperationCheckpoint gates checkpoint capture admission: a fresh\n132|\t// checkpoint is published under the current lease only.\n133|\tOperationCheckpoint Operation = \"checkpoint\"\n134|\t// OperationRestore gates terminal restore and the wrapper's first\n135|\t// start: ownership is compared before any provider resume.\n136|\tOperationRestore Operation = \"restore\"\n137|)\n138|\n139|// validOperation reports whether op names a gated action. Anything\n140|// else is a malformed gate call, never an authorized action.\n141|func validOperation(op Operation) bool {\n142|\tswitch op {\n143|\tcase OperationActivation, OperationInput, OperationMutation, OperationCheckpoint, OperationRestore:\n144|\t\treturn true\n145|\t}\n146|\treturn false\n147|}\n148|\n149|// launchClass reports whether op is a launch-class entry: activation\n150|// and restore park when ownership is remote, ambiguous, unverified,\n151|// or absent, while input, mutation, and checkpoint refuse outright.\n152|func launchClass(op Operation) bool {\n153|\treturn op == OperationActivation || op == OperationRestore\n154|}\n155|\n156|// PresentedToken is the caller's claimed fencing authority: the local\n157|// fencing token the wrapper compares, or the token a takeover, input,\n158|// mutation, or checkpoint caller holds. It is untrusted input: every\n159|// member is grammar-checked before any comparison runs.\n160|type PresentedToken struct {\n161|\tSessionID string\n162|\tEpoch     uint64\n163|\tLeaseID   string\n164|}\n165|\n166|// Observation carries the verified durable and sync facts the gate\n167|// decides over. Observe builds it from the repository; callers that\n168|// build it by hand (tests, modeled flows) must supply the same facts.\n169|// The winner is trusted only through its grammar: a malformed winning\n170|// summary refuses rather than authorizing against garbage.\n171|type Observation struct {\n172|\tSessionID string\n173|\t// Winner is the winning lease summary with its holder. It is\n174|\t// meaningful only when HasWinner is set.\n175|\tWinner    sessrepo.LeaseSummary\n176|\tHasWinner bool\n177|\t// LocalHostID is the host asking for authorization. An unknown or\n178|\t// empty local identity never equals the winning holder, so it\n179|\t// fails closed to the remote arm without a grammar check.\n180|\tLocalHostID string\n181|\t// Verified reports that a mesh lease refresh proved current\n182|\t// lease knowledge. Unverified ownership parks or refuses.\n183|\tVerified bool\n184|\t// Ambiguous reports conflicting ownership observations (a union\n185|\t// rival the local store cannot order). Ambiguity parks or refuses.\n186|\tAmbiguous bool\n187|\t// HandoffFailed reports that the caller's own handoff already\n188|\t// failed (a losing force lease before activation). A failed\n189|\t// handoff parks with failed_handoff instead of activating.\n190|\tHandoffFailed bool\n191|\t// Grant is the process-local authorization derived from a winning\n192|\t// lease, meaningful only when HasGrant is set. The gate re-checks\n193|\t// its expiry through the sessrepo owner on every call.\n194|\tGrant    sessrepo.FencingGrant\n195|\tHasGrant bool\n196|\t// Policy carries the configured lease refresh interval the\n197|\t// expiry arm enforces.\n198|\tPolicy sessrepo.FencingPolicy\n199|\t// Now is the caller's clock reading for the expiry arm. A grant\n200|\t// without a clock reading refuses rather than bypassing expiry.\n201|\tNow time.Time\n202|}\n203|\n204|// ObserveInput carries the caller-reported facts Observe combines with\n205|// the durable winning lease: sync state, handoff outcome, the\n206|// process-local fencing grant with its policy, and the clock reading.\n207|type ObserveInput struct {\n208|\tLocalHostID   string\n209|\tVerified      bool\n210|\tAmbiguous     bool\n211|\tHandoffFailed bool\n212|\tGrant         sessrepo.FencingGrant\n213|\tHasGrant      bool\n214|\tPolicy        sessrepo.FencingPolicy\n215|\tNow           time.Time\n216|}\n217|\n218|// Observe loads the winning lease for sessionID and combines it with\n219|// the caller's sync, handoff, grant, and clock facts into the\n220|// Observation Authorize decides over. The winner is the last summary\n221|// of the tuple-ordered ListLeases read, the same derivation\n222|// WinningLease returns, so no second winner rule exists here. A\n223|// session with no leases yet yields HasWinner false without an error:\n224|// absence is data the gate parks or refuses on. A repository failure\n225|// (including an unknown session) propagates unchanged.\n226|func Observe(repository *sessrepo.Repository, sessionID string, input ObserveInput) (Observation, error) {\n227|\tleases, err := repository.ListLeases(sessionID)\n228|\tif err != nil {\n229|\t\treturn Observation{}, err\n230|\t}\n231|\tobservation := Observation{\n232|\t\tSessionID:     sessionID,\n233|\t\tLocalHostID:   input.LocalHostID,\n234|\t\tVerified:      input.Verified,\n235|\t\tAmbiguous:     input.Ambiguous,\n236|\t\tHandoffFailed: input.HandoffFailed,\n237|\t\tGrant:         input.Grant,\n238|\t\tHasGrant:      input.HasGrant,\n239|\t\tPolicy:        input.Policy,\n240|\t\tNow:           input.Now,\n241|\t}\n242|\tif len(leases) > 0 {\n243|\t\tobservation.Winner = leases[len(leases)-1]\n244|\t\tobservation.HasWinner = true\n245|\t}\n246|\treturn observation, nil\n247|}\n248|\n249|// AuthorizeActivation gates provider activation and launch through the\n250|// fencing core.\n251|func AuthorizeActivation(presented PresentedToken, observation Observation) (LeaseToken, error) {\n252|\treturn Authorize(OperationActivation, presented, observation)\n253|}\n254|\n255|// AuthorizeInput gates provider input after attach through the fencing\n256|// core.\n257|func AuthorizeInput(presented PresentedToken, observation Observation) (LeaseToken, error) {\n258|\treturn Authorize(OperationInput, presented, observation)\n259|}\n260|\n261|// AuthorizeMutation gates owner-authored mutation through the fencing\n262|// core.\n263|func AuthorizeMutation(presented PresentedToken, observation Observation) (LeaseToken, error) {\n264|\treturn Authorize(OperationMutation, presented, observation)\n265|}\n266|\n267|// AuthorizeCheckpoint gates checkpoint capture admission through the\n268|// fencing core.\n269|func AuthorizeCheckpoint(presented PresentedToken, observation Observation) (LeaseToken, error) {\n270|\treturn Authorize(OperationCheckpoint, presented, observation)\n271|}\n272|\n273|// AuthorizeRestore gates terminal restore and the wrapper's first\n274|// start through the fencing core.\n275|func AuthorizeRestore(presented PresentedToken, observation Observation) (LeaseToken, error) {\n276|\treturn Authorize(OperationRestore, presented, observation)\n277|}\n278|\n279|// Authorize is the fencing core: every activation-class action passes\n280|// here. The presented token must name this session and equal the\n281|// winning (epoch, lease_id) tuple exactly; the fencing grant must be\n282|// present and unexpired; ownership must be verified, unambiguous, and\n283|// local. Launch-class entries (activation, restore) park with the\n284|// session.parked vocabulary when ownership is remote, ambiguous,\n285|// unverified, or absent; every other entry refuses outright. A passed\n286|// gate mints the sealed LeaseToken the provider operations bind; a\n287|// failed gate refuses with a Section 15 registered code and mints\n288|// nothing.\n289|//\n290|// Arm order is precedence: malformed calls die first, then foreign\n291|// sessions, then ownership presence and verifiability, then the\n292|// fencing grant, then ownership direction (the operative fact beats\n293|// the credential: a stale token under a remote winner parks remote,\n294|// it does not report stale), then the exact tuple match.\n295|func Authorize(operation Operation, presented PresentedToken, observation Observation) (LeaseToken, error) {\n296|\tif !validOperation(operation) {\n297|\t\treturn LeaseToken{}, refuse(ErrInvalidArguments, \"unknown fencing operation %q\", string(operation))\n298|\t}\n299|\tif _, err := scalar.ParseUUIDv7(presented.SessionID); err != nil {\n300|\t\treturn LeaseToken{}, refuse(ErrInvalidArguments, \"presented fencing token session %q is not a UUIDv7: %v\", presented.SessionID, err)\n301|\t}\n302|\tif presented.Epoch == 0 {\n303|\t\treturn LeaseToken{}, refuse(ErrInvalidArguments, \"presented fencing token carries epoch 0, want an epoch at or above 1\")\n304|\t}\n305|\tif _, err := scalar.ParseUUIDv4(presented.LeaseID); err != nil {\n306|\t\treturn LeaseToken{}, refuse(ErrInvalidArguments, \"presented fencing token lease %q is not a UUIDv4: %v\", presented.LeaseID, err)\n307|\t}\n308|\tif presented.SessionID != observation.SessionID {\n309|\t\treturn LeaseToken{}, refuse(ErrLeaseConflict, \"presented fencing token for session %s does not authorize session %s\", presented.SessionID, observation.SessionID)\n310|\t}\n311|\tif !observation.HasWinner {\n312|\t\tif launchClass(operation) {\n313|\t\t\treturn LeaseToken{}, park(ParkRestorePolicy, \"\", ErrLeaseConflict)\n314|\t\t}\n315|\t\treturn LeaseToken{}, refuse(ErrLeaseConflict, \"no winning lease is established for session %s\", observation.SessionID)\n316|\t}\n317|\tif observation.Winner.Epoch == 0 || !validLeaseID(observation.Winner.LeaseID) || !validHostID(observation.Winner.HolderHostID) {\n318|\t\treturn LeaseToken{}, refuse(ErrInvalidArguments, \"fencing observation for session %s carries no well-formed winning lease\", observation.SessionID)\n319|\t}\n320|\tif !observation.Verified {\n321|\t\tif launchClass(operation) {\n322|\t\t\treturn LeaseToken{}, park(ParkRestorePolicy, observation.Winner.LeaseID, ErrLeaseConflict)\n323|\t\t}\n324|\t\treturn LeaseToken{}, refuse(ErrLeaseConflict, \"ownership of session %s is unverified; refresh lease knowledge first\", observation.SessionID)\n325|\t}\n326|\tif observation.Ambiguous {\n327|\t\tif launchClass(operation) {\n328|\t\t\treturn LeaseToken{}, park(ParkRestorePolicy, observation.Winner.LeaseID, ErrLeaseConflict)\n329|\t\t}\n330|\t\treturn LeaseToken{}, refuse(ErrLeaseConflict, \"ownership of session %s is ambiguous; resolve the union rival first\", observation.SessionID)\n331|\t}\n332|\tif observation.HandoffFailed {\n333|\t\tif launchClass(operation) {\n334|\t\t\treturn LeaseToken{}, park(ParkFailedHandoff, observation.Winner.LeaseID, ErrLeaseConflict)\n335|\t\t}\n336|\t\treturn LeaseToken{}, refuse(ErrLeaseConflict, \"handoff for session %s already failed; a losing lease must never activate\", observation.SessionID)\n337|\t}\n338|\tif !observation.HasGrant {\n339|\t\treturn LeaseToken{}, refuse(ErrInvalidArguments, \"fencing observation for session %s carries no grant; validate the winning token first\", observation.SessionID)\n340|\t}\n341|\tif observation.Now.IsZero() {\n342|\t\treturn LeaseToken{}, refuse(ErrInvalidArguments, \"fencing observation for session %s carries no clock reading; expiry cannot be checked\", observation.SessionID)\n343|\t}\n344|\tif err := sessrepo.CheckFencingExpiry(observation.Grant, observation.Policy, observation.Now); err != nil {\n345|\t\tif errors.Is(err, sessrepo.ErrFencingExpired) {\n346|\t\t\treturn LeaseToken{}, refuse(ErrLeaseConflict, \"fencing grant for session %s lapsed; revalidate the winning token\", observation.SessionID)\n347|\t\t}\n348|\t\treturn LeaseToken{}, refuse(ErrInvalidArguments, \"fencing observation for session %s carries an unusable refresh policy\", observation.SessionID)\n349|\t}\n350|\tif observation.Winner.HolderHostID != observation.LocalHostID {\n351|\t\tif launchClass(operation) {\n352|\t\t\treturn LeaseToken{}, park(ParkRemoteOwner, observation.Winner.LeaseID, ErrNotOwner)\n353|\t\t}\n354|\t\treturn LeaseToken{}, refuse(ErrNotOwner, \"session %s is owned by remote host %s\", observation.SessionID, observation.Winner.HolderHostID)\n355|\t}\n356|\tepochsEqual := presented.Epoch == observation.Winner.Epoch\n357|\tif !epochsEqual {\n358|\t\tif presented.Epoch < observation.Winner.Epoch {\n359|\t\t\tif launchClass(operation) {\n360|\t\t\t\treturn LeaseToken{}, park(ParkStaleOwner, observation.Winner.LeaseID, ErrStaleOwner)\n361|\t\t\t}\n362|\t\t\treturn LeaseToken{}, refuse(ErrStaleOwner, \"presented epoch %d precedes winning epoch %d for session %s\", presented.Epoch, observation.Winner.Epoch, observation.SessionID)\n363|\t\t}\n364|\t\tif launchClass(operation) {\n365|\t\t\treturn LeaseToken{}, park(ParkRestorePolicy, observation.Winner.LeaseID, ErrLeaseConflict)\n366|\t\t}\n367|\t\treturn LeaseToken{}, refuse(ErrLeaseConflict, \"presented epoch %d names no known lease for session %s\", presented.Epoch, observation.SessionID)\n368|\t}\n369|\tif presented.LeaseID != observation.Winner.LeaseID {\n370|\t\tif launchClass(operation) {\n371|\t\t\treturn LeaseToken{}, park(ParkStaleOwner, observation.Winner.LeaseID, ErrLeaseConflict)\n372|\t\t}\n373|\t\treturn LeaseToken{}, refuse(ErrLeaseConflict, \"presented lease %s loses to winning lease %s at epoch %d\", presented.LeaseID, observation.Winner.LeaseID, observation.Winner.Epoch)\n374|\t}\n375|\treturn mintLeaseToken(observation.SessionID, observation.Winner.Epoch, observation.Winner.LeaseID), nil\n376|}\n377|\n378|// validLeaseID reports whether id parses as a fencing token UUID. The\n379|// scalar owner holds the grammar; this is only the boolean access the\n380|// combined winner arm needs.\n381|func validLeaseID(id string) bool {\n382|\t_, err := scalar.ParseUUIDv4(id)\n383|\treturn err == nil\n384|}\n385|\n386|// validHostID reports whether id parses as a host UUID. The scalar\n387|// owner holds the grammar; this is only the boolean access the\n388|// combined winner arm needs.\n389|func validHostID(id string) bool {\n390|\t_, err := scalar.ParseUUIDv7(id)\n391|\treturn err == nil\n392|}","final_result":true}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c699","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b2ff-60d1-7b92-bcfc-8a4c766633f3"},"sequence":423,"recorded_at":1780531400000841,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"b5be48e9-caa3-42a3-a29a-786d769c2b71","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"b5be48e9-caa3-42a3-a29a-786d769c2b71","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"b5be48e9-caa3-42a3-a29a-786d769c2b71"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b300-9fdf-7aa2-b6f9-ec316583640c"},"task_id":"01a0b300-9fdf-7aa2-b6f9-ec316583640c","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"01a0b300-9fdf-7aa2-b6f9-ec316583640c"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c69b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b2ff-60d1-7b92-bcfc-8a4c766633f3"},"sequence":424,"recorded_at":1780531400000843,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"b5be48e9-caa3-42a3-a29a-786d769c2b71","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"b5be48e9-caa3-42a3-a29a-786d769c2b71","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"b5be48e9-caa3-42a3-a29a-786d769c2b71"},"call_id":"call_01a0b3009c9674c2a4efbd3b665ae68f","text":"Read text file `internal/terminstance/fencing.go`.\n1|package terminstance\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/fencing\"\n5|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/terminalbackend\"\n6|)\n7|\n8|// ObserveFencing projects one AX fencing observation onto the Terminal\n9|// Instance lifecycle. It is the ONLY entry that produces stale_fenced:\n10|// no backend operation targets that state (the landed CheckTransition\n11|// proves it and the engine never synthesizes it), only AX fencing\n12|// observation does.\n13|//\n14|// The verdict is read entirely from the landed fencing projection: the\n15|// presented local token is authorized against the observation through\n16|// fencing.Authorize with the restore operation, and a ParkStaleOwner\n17|// park — the older-epoch arm and the same-epoch lease-mismatch arm\n18|// alike — moves the local observation to stale_fenced. The operation\n19|// must be launch-class (restore or activation): the input, mutation\n20|// and checkpoint entries refuse a stale token instead of parking it,\n21|// which would surface as an error and never fence. Restore is chosen\n22|// over activation because it gates terminal restore, this story's\n23|// domain; the two are equivalent on the stale arms.\n24|//\n25|// A stale token under a REMOTE winner fences too: the landed gate parks\n26|// remote_owner before it compares tuples (\"the operative fact beats the\n27|// credential\"), so the first verdict cannot distinguish a stale token\n28|// from the winning token under a foreign winner. The second question\n29|// asks the landed gate whether the presented token is stale RELATIVE TO\n30|// THE WINNER by authorizing from the winner's own host (LocalHostID set\n31|// to Winner.HolderHostID) and reading the park: stale_owner fences,\n32|// anything else — including the winning token authorizing cleanly —\n33|// leaves the state with the original remote park. Both questions run\n34|// inside the landed Authorize; no local tuple comparison exists here.\n35|//\n36|// Only a live incarnation fences: creating, parked, active and\n37|// quiescing move to stale_fenced, while absent and stopped (no\n38|// incarnation exists for terminate-stale to target), stale_fenced\n39|// itself (already fenced: the transition is idempotent) and\n40|// unavailable (the observation is unknown and no verdict is projected\n41|// over unknown) surface the park with no transition. Every other\n42|// outcome leaves the state untouched: an authorized token reports no\n43|// transition, and any non-stale refusal or park (unverified, ambiguous,\n44|// no winner) surfaces its own error with no transition, because only\n45|// proven staleness fences. A nil error with transitioned false is the\n46|// authorized case.\n47|//\n48|// This function performs no lease comparison of its own: the tuple,\n49|// grant, expiry and direction arms all run inside the landed Authorize,\n50|// so no second fencing model exists here. It reads Winner.LeaseID and\n51|// Winner.Epoch only through Authorize's verdict, never Winner.Checkpoint:\n52|// lease records are immutable content-addressed blobs whose checkpoint\n53|// member is null for every epoch-1 lease, so keying on it would be\n54|// vacuous for every session that never changed hands.\n55|func ObserveFencing(current terminalbackend.InstanceState, presented fencing.PresentedToken, observation fencing.Observation) (terminalbackend.InstanceState, bool, error) {\n56|\tif _, err := terminalbackend.ParseInstanceState(string(current)); err != nil {\n57|\t\treturn current, false, wrapLanded(err)\n58|\t}\n59|\t_, authErr := fencing.Authorize(fencing.OperationRestore, presented, observation)\n60|\tif authErr == nil {\n61|\t\treturn current, false, nil\n62|\t}\n63|\treason, _, parked := fencing.ParkDetails(authErr)\n64|\tif parked && reason == fencing.ParkRemoteOwner {\n65|\t\treturn observeRemoteWinner(current, presented, observation, authErr)\n66|\t}\n67|\tif parked && reason == fencing.ParkStaleOwner {\n68|\t\treturn fenceLive(current, authErr)\n69|\t}\n70|\treturn current, false, authErr\n71|}\n72|\n73|// observeRemoteWinner resolves a remote-winner park: the winner is on\n74|// another host and the presented token may be stale relative to it (the\n75|// force-takeover case) or the winning token itself observed from afar.\n76|// The landed gate decides from the winner's own host; only a stale\n77|// verdict fences, and only from a live incarnation.\n78|func observeRemoteWinner(current terminalbackend.InstanceState, presented fencing.PresentedToken, observation fencing.Observation, authErr error) (terminalbackend.InstanceState, bool, error) {\n79|\trelative := observation\n80|\trelative.LocalHostID = observation.Winner.HolderHostID\n81|\t_, relativeErr := fencing.Authorize(fencing.OperationRestore, presented, relative)\n82|\tif relativeErr == nil {\n83|\t\treturn current, false, authErr\n84|\t}\n85|\tif relativeReason, _, relativeParked := fencing.ParkDetails(relativeErr); relativeParked && relativeReason == fencing.ParkStaleOwner {\n86|\t\treturn fenceLive(current, authErr)\n87|\t}\n88|\treturn current, false, authErr\n89|}\n90|\n91|// fenceLive moves a live incarnation to stale_fenced and leaves every\n92|// other source untouched with the park that proved staleness. Absent\n93|// and stopped name no incarnation, stale_fenced is already fenced, and\n94|// unavailable is unknown: none of them transitions.\n95|func fenceLive(current terminalbackend.InstanceState, authErr error) (terminalbackend.InstanceState, bool, error) {\n96|\tswitch current {\n97|\tcase terminalbackend.StateCreating, terminalbackend.StateParked,\n98|\t\tterminalbackend.StateActive, terminalbackend.StateQuiescing:\n99|\t\treturn terminalbackend.StateStaleFenced, true, nil\n100|\tdefault:\n101|\t\treturn current, false, authErr\n102|\t}\n103|}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c69d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b2ff-60d1-7b92-bcfc-8a4c766633f3"},"sequence":425,"recorded_at":1780531400000845,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"b5be48e9-caa3-42a3-a29a-786d769c2b71","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"b5be48e9-caa3-42a3-a29a-786d769c2b71","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"b5be48e9-caa3-42a3-a29a-786d769c2b71"},"call_id":"call_01a0b3009db97782b21df837d8a9b9cd","text":"Read text file `internal/fencing/gate.go`.\n1|package fencing\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"errors\"\n5|\t\"fmt\"\n6|\t\"time\"\n7|\n8|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/scalar\"\n9|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/sessrepo\"\n10|)\n11|\n12|var (\n13|\t// ErrLeaseConflict is the Section 15 lease_conflict refusal at exit\n14|\t// 10: the presented fencing proof is not the winning authority for\n15|\t// this session (same-epoch loser, epoch beyond the winner, foreign\n16|\t// session, lapsed grant, or absent/ambiguous/unverified ownership on\n17|\t// a non-launch entry), or a forged capability reached a consumer.\n18|\tErrLeaseConflict = errors.New(\"lease_conflict\")\n19|\t// ErrNotOwner is the Section 15 not_owner refusal at exit 10: the\n20|\t// winning lease holder is a remote host and this entry is not a\n21|\t// launch, so there is no parked direction to take.\n22|\tErrNotOwner = errors.New(\"not_owner\")\n23|\t// ErrStaleOwner is the Section 15 stale_owner refusal at exit 10:\n24|\t// the presented epoch precedes the winning epoch on a non-launch\n25|\t// entry. Launch entries park with the stale_owner reason instead.\n26|\tErrStaleOwner = errors.New(\"stale_owner\")\n27|\t// ErrParked marks a park decision: the launch is refused and the\n28|\t// session must park carrying the session.parked reason and winning\n29|\t// lease ID. It always wraps the underlying Section 15 cause as\n30|\t// well, so errors.Is reports both the decision and the class.\n31|\tErrParked = errors.New(\"parked\")\n32|\t// ErrInvalidArguments is the Section 15 invalid_arguments refusal\n33|\t// at exit 2: the gate call itself is malformed (unknown operation,\n34|\t// malformed presented token or winning summary, missing grant,\n35|\t// missing clock reading, unusable policy, or unknown provider\n36|\t// operation). The caller fixes the call, not the ownership.\n37|\tErrInvalidArguments = errors.New(\"invalid_arguments\")\n38|\t// ErrLocalPreconditionFailed is the Section 15\n39|\t// local_precondition_failed refusal at exit 3, the class the\n40|\t// Section 4.C terminate-stale row names: terminate-stale without\n41|\t// explicit force recovery, without preserved diagnostics, without\n42|\t// an established winner, or against the live winning owner.\n43|\tErrLocalPreconditionFailed = errors.New(\"local_precondition_failed\")\n44|)\n45|\n46|// refuse is the single refusal funnel every fencing rejection flows\n47|// through. No production path wraps a sentinel with fmt.Errorf directly.\n48|var refuse = func(sentinel error, format string, arguments ...any) error {\n49|\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"%w: %s\", sentinel, fmt.Sprintf(format, arguments...))\n50|}\n51|\n52|// ParkReason is one Section 5.2 session.parked reason: the exact\n53|// vocabulary a park decision carries.\n54|type ParkReason string\n55|\n56|const (\n57|\t// ParkRemoteOwner parks because the winning lease holder is remote.\n58|\tParkRemoteOwner ParkReason = \"remote_owner\"\n59|\t// ParkStaleOwner parks because the local fencing proof loses to the\n60|\t// winning lease while the winner is local (a stale cache).\n61|\tParkStaleOwner ParkReason = \"stale_owner\"\n62|\t// ParkRestorePolicy parks because ownership cannot be verified:\n63|\t// no winning lease, unverified sync, ambiguous observations, or a\n64|\t// token from an epoch beyond the winner.\n65|\tParkRestorePolicy ParkReason = \"restore_policy\"\n66|\t// ParkFailedHandoff parks because the caller's handoff already\n67|\t// failed: a losing force lease must never activate.\n68|\tParkFailedHandoff ParkReason = \"failed_handoff\"\n69|)\n70|\n71|// parkRefusal carries a park decision: the session.parked reason, the\n72|// winning lease ID the parked event repeats (empty when no winner is\n73|// established), and the underlying Section 15 cause. It unwraps to both\n74|// ErrParked and the cause.\n75|type parkRefusal struct {\n76|\treason         ParkReason\n77|\twinningLeaseID string\n78|\tcause          error\n79|}\n80|\n81|func (refusal *parkRefusal) Error() string {\n82|\tif refusal.winningLeaseID == \"\" {\n83|\t\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"%s: park (%s); no winning lease is established\", ErrParked, refusal.reason)\n84|\t}\n85|\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"%s: park (%s) under winning lease %s: %v\", ErrParked, refusal.reason, refusal.winningLeaseID, refusal.cause)\n86|}\n87|\n88|func (refusal *parkRefusal) Unwrap() []error {\n89|\treturn []error{ErrParked, refusal.cause}\n90|}\n91|\n92|// IsParked reports whether err is a park decision rather than a hard\n93|// refusal. A parked launch must emit the session.parked vocabulary,\n94|// never start a runtime.\n95|func IsParked(err error) bool {\n96|\treturn errors.Is(err, ErrParked)\n97|}\n98|\n99|// ParkDetails extracts the session.parked vocabulary from a park\n100|// decision: the reason and the winning lease ID (empty when no winner\n101|// is established). It reports false for a hard refusal.\n102|func ParkDetails(err error) (ParkReason, string, bool) {\n103|\tvar parked *parkRefusal\n104|\tif !errors.As(err, &parked) {\n105|\t\treturn \"\", \"\", false\n106|\t}\n107|\treturn parked.reason, parked.winningLeaseID, true\n108|}\n109|\n110|// park builds the launch-class refusal for one ownership condition: the\n111|// parked reason with the Section 15 cause the same condition refuses\n112|// on a non-launch entry.\n113|func park(reason ParkReason, winningLeaseID string, cause error) error {\n114|\treturn &parkRefusal{reason: reason, winningLeaseID: winningLeaseID, cause: cause}\n115|}\n116|\n117|// Operation is one activation-class action the gate authorizes.\n118|type Operation string\n119|\n120|const (\n121|\t// OperationActivation gates provider activation and launch: only\n122|\t// the winning committed lease may create a destination runtime.\n123|\tOperationActivation Operation = \"activation\"\n124|\t// OperationInput gates provider input after attach (the\n125|\t// quiesce-input and attach direction): the owner revalidates\n126|\t// before accepting operator input.\n127|\tOperationInput Operation = \"input\"\n128|\t// OperationMutation gates owner-authored mutation: event append\n129|\t// and compare-and-swap succession carry the winning epoch.\n130|\tOperationMutation Operation = \"mutation\"\n131|\t// OperationCheckpoint gates checkpoint capture admission: a fresh\n132|\t// checkpoint is published under the current lease only.\n133|\tOperationCheckpoint Operation = \"checkpoint\"\n134|\t// OperationRestore gates terminal restore and the wrapper's first\n135|\t// start: ownership is compared before any provider resume.\n136|\tOperationRestore Operation = \"restore\"\n137|)\n138|\n139|// validOperation reports whether op names a gated action. Anything\n140|// else is a malformed gate call, never an authorized action.\n141|func validOperation(op Operation) bool {\n142|\tswitch op {\n143|\tcase OperationActivation, OperationInput, OperationMutation, OperationCheckpoint, OperationRestore:\n144|\t\treturn true\n145|\t}\n146|\treturn false\n147|}\n148|\n149|// launchClass reports whether op is a launch-class entry: activation\n150|// and restore park when ownership is remote, ambiguous, unverified,\n151|// or absent, while input, mutation, and checkpoint refuse outright.\n152|func launchClass(op Operation) bool {\n153|\treturn op == OperationActivation || op == OperationRestore\n154|}\n155|\n156|// PresentedToken is the caller's claimed fencing authority: the local\n157|// fencing token the wrapper compares, or the token a takeover, input,\n158|// mutation, or checkpoint caller holds. It is untrusted input: every\n159|// member is grammar-checked before any comparison runs.\n160|type PresentedToken struct {\n161|\tSessionID string\n162|\tEpoch     uint64\n163|\tLeaseID   string\n164|}\n165|\n166|// Observation carries the verified durable and sync facts the gate\n167|// decides over. Observe builds it from the repository; callers that\n168|// build it by hand (tests, modeled flows) must supply the same facts.\n169|// The winner is trusted only through its grammar: a malformed winning\n170|// summary refuses rather than authorizing against garbage.\n171|type Observation struct {\n172|\tSessionID string\n173|\t// Winner is the winning lease summary with its holder. It is\n174|\t// meaningful only when HasWinner is set.\n175|\tWinner    sessrepo.LeaseSummary\n176|\tHasWinner bool\n177|\t// LocalHostID is the host asking for authorization. An unknown or\n178|\t// empty local identity never equals the winning holder, so it\n179|\t// fails closed to the remote arm without a grammar check.\n180|\tLocalHostID string\n181|\t// Verified reports that a mesh lease refresh proved current\n182|\t// lease knowledge. Unverified ownership parks or refuses.\n183|\tVerified bool\n184|\t// Ambiguous reports conflicting ownership observations (a union\n185|\t// rival the local store cannot order). Ambiguity parks or refuses.\n186|\tAmbiguous bool\n187|\t// HandoffFailed reports that the caller's own handoff already\n188|\t// failed (a losing force lease before activation). A failed\n189|\t// handoff parks with failed_handoff instead of activating.\n190|\tHandoffFailed bool\n191|\t// Grant is the process-local authorization derived from a winning\n192|\t// lease, meaningful only when HasGrant is set. The gate re-checks\n193|\t// its expiry through the sessrepo owner on every call.\n194|\tGrant    sessrepo.FencingGrant\n195|\tHasGrant bool\n196|\t// Policy carries the configured lease refresh interval the\n197|\t// expiry arm enforces.\n198|\tPolicy sessrepo.FencingPolicy\n199|\t// Now is the caller's clock reading for the expiry arm. A grant\n200|\t// without a clock reading refuses rather than bypassing expiry.\n201|\tNow time.Time\n202|}\n203|\n204|// ObserveInput carries the caller-reported facts Observe combines with\n205|// the durable winning lease: sync state, handoff outcome, the\n206|// process-local fencing grant with its policy, and the clock reading.\n207|type ObserveInput struct {\n208|\tLocalHostID   string\n209|\tVerified      bool\n210|\tAmbiguous     bool\n211|\tHandoffFailed bool\n212|\tGrant         sessrepo.FencingGrant\n213|\tHasGrant      bool\n214|\tPolicy        sessrepo.FencingPolicy\n215|\tNow           time.Time\n216|}\n217|\n218|// Observe loads the winning lease for sessionID and combines it with\n219|// the caller's sync, handoff, grant, and clock facts into the\n220|// Observation Authorize decides over. The winner is the last summary\n221|// of the tuple-ordered ListLeases read, the same derivation\n222|// WinningLease returns, so no second winner rule exists here. A\n223|// session with no leases yet yields HasWinner false without an error:\n224|// absence is data the gate parks or refuses on. A repository failure\n225|// (including an unknown session) propagates unchanged.\n226|func Observe(repository *sessrepo.Repository, sessionID string, input ObserveInput) (Observation, error) {\n227|\tleases, err := repository.ListLeases(sessionID)\n228|\tif err != nil {\n229|\t\treturn Observation{}, err\n230|\t}\n231|\tobservation := Observation{\n232|\t\tSessionID:     sessionID,\n233|\t\tLocalHostID:   input.LocalHostID,\n234|\t\tVerified:      input.Verified,\n235|\t\tAmbiguous:     input.Ambiguous,\n236|\t\tHandoffFailed: input.HandoffFailed,\n237|\t\tGrant:         input.Grant,\n238|\t\tHasGrant:      input.HasGrant,\n239|\t\tPolicy:        input.Policy,\n240|\t\tNow:           input.Now,\n241|\t}\n242|\tif len(leases) > 0 {\n243|\t\tobservation.Winner = leases[len(leases)-1]\n244|\t\tobservation.HasWinner = true\n245|\t}\n246|\treturn observation, nil\n247|}\n248|\n249|// AuthorizeActivation gates provider activation and launch through the\n250|// fencing core.\n251|func AuthorizeActivation(presented PresentedToken, observation Observation) (LeaseToken, error) {\n252|\treturn Authorize(OperationActivation, presented, observation)\n253|}\n254|\n255|// AuthorizeInput gates provider input after attach through the fencing\n256|// core.\n257|func AuthorizeInput(presented PresentedToken, observation Observation) (LeaseToken, error) {\n258|\treturn Authorize(OperationInput, presented, observation)\n259|}\n260|\n261|// AuthorizeMutation gates owner-authored mutation through the fencing\n262|// core.\n263|func AuthorizeMutation(presented PresentedToken, observation Observation) (LeaseToken, error) {\n264|\treturn Authorize(OperationMutation, presented, observation)\n265|}\n266|\n267|// AuthorizeCheckpoint gates checkpoint capture admission through the\n268|// fencing core.\n269|func AuthorizeCheckpoint(presented PresentedToken, observation Observation) (LeaseToken, error) {\n270|\treturn Authorize(OperationCheckpoint, presented, observation)\n271|}\n272|\n273|// AuthorizeRestore gates terminal restore and the wrapper's first\n274|// start through the fencing core.\n275|func AuthorizeRestore(presented PresentedToken, observation Observation) (LeaseToken, error) {\n276|\treturn Authorize(OperationRestore, presented, observation)\n277|}\n278|\n279|// Authorize is the fencing core: every activation-class action passes\n280|// here. The presented token must name this session and equal the\n281|// winning (epoch, lease_id) tuple exactly; the fencing grant must be\n282|// present and unexpired; ownership must be verified, unambiguous, and\n283|// local. Launch-class entries (activation, restore) park with the\n284|// session.parked vocabulary when ownership is remote, ambiguous,\n285|// unverified, or absent; every other entry refuses outright. A passed\n286|// gate mints the sealed LeaseToken the provider operations bind; a\n287|// failed gate refuses with a Section 15 registered code and mints\n288|// nothing.\n289|//\n290|// Arm order is precedence: malformed calls die first, then foreign\n291|// sessions, then ownership presence and verifiability, then the\n292|// fencing grant, then ownership direction (the operative fact beats\n293|// the credential: a stale token under a remote winner parks remote,\n294|// it does not report stale), then the exact tuple match.\n295|func Authorize(operation Operation, presented PresentedToken, observation Observation) (LeaseToken, error) {\n296|\tif !validOperation(operation) {\n297|\t\treturn LeaseToken{}, refuse(ErrInvalidArguments, \"unknown fencing operation %q\", string(operation))\n298|\t}\n299|\tif _, err := scalar.ParseUUIDv7(presented.SessionID); err != nil {\n300|\t\treturn LeaseToken{}, refuse(ErrInvalidArguments, \"presented fencing token session %q is not a UUIDv7: %v\", presented.SessionID, err)\n301|\t}\n302|\tif presented.Epoch == 0 {\n303|\t\treturn LeaseToken{}, refuse(ErrInvalidArguments, \"presented fencing token carries epoch 0, want an epoch at or above 1\")\n304|\t}\n305|\tif _, err := scalar.ParseUUIDv4(presented.LeaseID); err != nil {\n306|\t\treturn LeaseToken{}, refuse(ErrInvalidArguments, \"presented fencing token lease %q is not a UUIDv4: %v\", presented.LeaseID, err)\n307|\t}\n308|\tif presented.SessionID != observation.SessionID {\n309|\t\treturn LeaseToken{}, refuse(ErrLeaseConflict, \"presented fencing token for session %s does not authorize session %s\", presented.SessionID, observation.SessionID)\n310|\t}\n311|\tif !observation.HasWinner {\n312|\t\tif launchClass(operation) {\n313|\t\t\treturn LeaseToken{}, park(ParkRestorePolicy, \"\", ErrLeaseConflict)\n314|\t\t}\n315|\t\treturn LeaseToken{}, refuse(ErrLeaseConflict, \"no winning lease is established for session %s\", observation.SessionID)\n316|\t}\n317|\tif observation.Winner.Epoch == 0 || !validLeaseID(observation.Winner.LeaseID) || !validHostID(observation.Winner.HolderHostID) {\n318|\t\treturn LeaseToken{}, refuse(ErrInvalidArguments, \"fencing observation for session %s carries no well-formed winning lease\", observation.SessionID)\n319|\t}\n320|\tif !observation.Verified {\n321|\t\tif launchClass(operation) {\n322|\t\t\treturn LeaseToken{}, park(ParkRestorePolicy, observation.Winner.LeaseID, ErrLeaseConflict)\n323|\t\t}\n324|\t\treturn LeaseToken{}, refuse(ErrLeaseConflict, \"ownership of session %s is unverified; refresh lease knowledge first\", observation.SessionID)\n325|\t}\n326|\tif observation.Ambiguous {\n327|\t\tif launchClass(operation) {\n328|\t\t\treturn LeaseToken{}, park(ParkRestorePolicy, observation.Winner.LeaseID, ErrLeaseConflict)\n329|\t\t}\n330|\t\treturn LeaseToken{}, refuse(ErrLeaseConflict, \"ownership of session %s is ambiguous; resolve the union rival first\", observation.SessionID)\n331|\t}\n332|\tif observation.HandoffFailed {\n333|\t\tif launchClass(operation) {\n334|\t\t\treturn LeaseToken{}, park(ParkFailedHandoff, observation.Winner.LeaseID, ErrLeaseConflict)\n335|\t\t}\n336|\t\treturn LeaseToken{}, refuse(ErrLeaseConflict, \"handoff for session %s already failed; a losing lease must never activate\", observation.SessionID)\n337|\t}\n338|\tif !observation.HasGrant {\n339|\t\treturn LeaseToken{}, refuse(ErrInvalidArguments, \"fencing observation for session %s carries no grant; validate the winning token first\", observation.SessionID)\n340|\t}\n341|\tif observation.Now.IsZero() {\n342|\t\treturn LeaseToken{}, refuse(ErrInvalidArguments, \"fencing observation for session %s carries no clock reading; expiry cannot be checked\", observation.SessionID)\n343|\t}\n344|\tif err := sessrepo.CheckFencingExpiry(observation.Grant, observation.Policy, observation.Now); err != nil {\n345|\t\tif errors.Is(err, sessrepo.ErrFencingExpired) {\n346|\t\t\treturn LeaseToken{}, refuse(ErrLeaseConflict, \"fencing grant for session %s lapsed; revalidate the winning token\", observation.SessionID)\n347|\t\t}\n348|\t\treturn LeaseToken{}, refuse(ErrInvalidArguments, \"fencing observation for session %s carries an unusable refresh policy\", observation.SessionID)\n349|\t}\n350|\tif observation.Winner.HolderHostID != observation.LocalHostID {\n351|\t\tif launchClass(operation) {\n352|\t\t\treturn LeaseToken{}, park(ParkRemoteOwner, observation.Winner.LeaseID, ErrNotOwner)\n353|\t\t}\n354|\t\treturn LeaseToken{}, refuse(ErrNotOwner, \"session %s is owned by remote host %s\", observation.SessionID, observation.Winner.HolderHostID)\n355|\t}\n356|\tepochsEqual := presented.Epoch == observation.Winner.Epoch\n357|\tif !epochsEqual {\n358|\t\tif presented.Epoch < observation.Winner.Epoch {\n359|\t\t\tif launchClass(operation) {\n360|\t\t\t\treturn LeaseToken{}, park(ParkStaleOwner, observation.Winner.LeaseID, ErrStaleOwner)\n361|\t\t\t}\n362|\t\t\treturn LeaseToken{}, refuse(ErrStaleOwner, \"presented epoch %d precedes winning epoch %d for session %s\", presented.Epoch, observation.Winner.Epoch, observation.SessionID)\n363|\t\t}\n364|\t\tif launchClass(operation) {\n365|\t\t\treturn LeaseToken{}, park(ParkRestorePolicy, observation.Winner.LeaseID, ErrLeaseConflict)\n366|\t\t}\n367|\t\treturn LeaseToken{}, refuse(ErrLeaseConflict, \"presented epoch %d names no known lease for session %s\", presented.Epoch, observation.SessionID)\n368|\t}\n369|\tif presented.LeaseID != observation.Winner.LeaseID {\n370|\t\tif launchClass(operation) {\n371|\t\t\treturn LeaseToken{}, park(ParkStaleOwner, observation.Winner.LeaseID, ErrLeaseConflict)\n372|\t\t}\n373|\t\treturn LeaseToken{}, refuse(ErrLeaseConflict, \"presented lease %s loses to winning lease %s at epoch %d\", presented.LeaseID, observation.Winner.LeaseID, observation.Winner.Epoch)\n374|\t}\n375|\treturn mintLeaseToken(observation.SessionID, observation.Winner.Epoch, observation.Winner.LeaseID), nil\n376|}\n377|\n378|// validLeaseID reports whether id parses as a fencing token UUID. The\n379|// scalar owner holds the grammar; this is only the boolean access the\n380|// combined winner arm needs.\n381|func validLeaseID(id string) bool {\n382|\t_, err := scalar.ParseUUIDv4(id)\n383|\treturn err == nil\n384|}\n385|\n386|// validHostID reports whether id parses as a host UUID. The scalar\n387|// owner holds the grammar; this is only the boolean access the\n388|// combined winner arm needs.\n389|func validHostID(id string) bool {\n390|\t_, err := scalar.ParseUUIDv7(id)\n391|\treturn err == nil\n392|}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
