third | Per-effect auth recheck (pre-third skipped) | `TestExecuteRechecksBeforeThirdEffect/lease_rotates_before_third_effect` |\n231|| N-engine-recheck-generation-third | Per-effect generation recheck (pre-third skipped) | `TestExecuteRechecksBeforeThirdEffect/generation_rotates_before_third_effect` |\n232|| N-engine-bind-prelink | Pre-link restore skipped for quiesce | `TestExecutePreLinkStoreFailureRestoresSource` |\n233|| N-engine-bind-postlink | Standing receipt restores source | `TestExecuteHookErrorRetryReconcilesThroughStatus/standing_receipt_is_uncertain` |\n234|| N-resume-status-error | Resumption on timed-out reconciliation read | `TestExecuteUncertainRetryUnknownObservationRefuses/coded_read_failure` |\n235|| N-resume-contradiction | Resumption on parked contradiction | `TestExecuteUncertainRetryTargetProvenRefuses/contradictory_observation` |\n236|| N-resume-target | Resumption on proven target | `TestExecuteUncertainRetryTargetProvenRefuses/quiesce_target_proven` |\n237|| N-resume-scope-instance | Reconciliation through session-scoped lookup | `TestExecuteUncertainRetryUnknownObservationRefuses/lying_match_on_drifted_instance` |\n238|| N-resume-complete-key | Completion under a second key | `TestExecuteIdenticalRetryReplays` |\n239|| N-resume-generation-value | Reconciliation with empty generation | `TestExecuteUncertainRetryResumesWhenStatusProvesSource` |\n240|| N-status-session-scoped | Session comparison skipped (session-scoped) | `TestExecuteStatusSessionDriftRefuses/session_scoped_lying_match_refuses` |\n241|| N-status-session-exact | Session comparison skipped (exact) | `TestExecuteStatusSessionDriftRefuses/exact_lying_match_refuses` |\n242|| N-status-match-instance | Match conjunction loses instance | `TestExecuteStatusIdentityMatchEachAxis/instance/lying_match_refuses` |\n243|| N-status-match-backend | Match conjunction loses backend | `TestExecuteStatusIdentityMatchEachAxis/backend/lying_match_refuses` |\n244|| N-status-match-implementation | Match conjunction loses implementation | `TestExecuteStatusIdentityMatchEachAxis/implementation/lying_match_refuses` |\n245|| N-status-match-protocol | Match conjunction loses protocol | `TestExecuteStatusIdentityMatchEachAxis/protocol/lying_match_refuses` |\n246|| N-status-match-generation | Match conjunction loses generation | `TestExecuteStatusIdentityMatchEachAxis/generation/lying_match_refuses` |\n247|| N-engine-deadline-instant | Entry deadline admits the instant | `TestExecuteEntryDeadlineInstantRefuses` |\n248|| N-status-deadline-instant | Status deadline admits the instant | `TestExecuteStatusDeadlineInstantRefuses` |\n249|| N-auth-kind-attach | Kind vocabulary admits attach | `TestParseAuthorizationKindClosed` |\n250|| N-auth-kind-none | Kind vocabulary admits none | `TestParseAuthorizationKindClosed` |\n251|| N-engine-recheck-auth | Per-effect auth recheck (pre-first skipped) | `TestExecuteRechecksBeforeEachEffect/rotation_before_first_effect_restores_source` |\n252|| N-engine-recheck-generation | Per-effect generation recheck (pre-first skipped) | `TestExecuteRechecksBeforeEachEffect/generation_rotation_before_first_effect_restores_source` |\n253|| N-engine-precommit-after | Pre-commit after-state (timeouts to unavailable) | `TestExecutePreEffectErrorsRestoreSource/coded_backend_refusal_on_first_effect` |\n254|| N-engine-postcommit-after | Post-commit after-state (process failures to source) | `TestExecutePostEffectErrorsMoveUnavailable/coded_refusal_on_second_effect` |\n255|| N-engine-status-match | Status match equality (absent-state lies) | `TestExecuteStatusMatchedTupleFalseFormRefuses` |\n256|| N-engine-status-unknown | Status unknown (uncoded reported absent) | `TestExecuteStatusUnknownIsNeverAbsent` |\n257|| N-engine-status-conditional | Status provider conditional (fixture backend) | `TestExecuteStatusProviderConditional` |\n258|| N-status-nullpair | Status null-pair rule (one half) | `TestParseStatusBodyNullPairRule` |\n259|| N-interim | Interim creating (quiesce too) | `TestExecuteInterimState` |\n260|| N-engine-kind-map | Kind mapping (landed control honored as create) | `TestExecuteQuiesceSuccess` |\n261|| N-fencing-operation | Fencing op must be launch-class (mutation refuses stale) | `TestObserveFencingStaleEpochFences` |\n262|| N-engine-timeout-code-stop | Row timeout code (stop reports quiesce code) | `TestExecuteEntryDeadlineCodes/request-stop` |\n263|| N-engine-timeout-code-default | Row timeout code (default reports stop code) | `TestExecuteEntryDeadlineCodes/quiesce-input` |\n264|| N-engine-status-source | Status source matrix (garbage admitted) | `TestExecuteStatusAllSources` |\n265|| N-params-bootstrap | Params bootstrap (admits nope) | `TestCheckMutationContextParams` |\n266|| N-params-quiescence-quiesce | Params quiescence quiesce-arm (admits nope) | `TestCheckMutationContextParams` |\n267|| N-params-quiescence-wait | Params quiescence wait-arm (admits nope) | `TestCheckMutationContextParams` |\n268|| N-params-proof | Params proof (admits provider_restart) | `TestCheckMutationContextParams` |\n269|| N-params-evidence | Params stop evidence (admits not-a-digest) | `TestCheckMutationContextParams` |\n270|| N-params-graceful | Params graceful bound (admits 3600001) | `TestCheckMutationContextParams` |\n271|| N-version-delegation | Version-tuple delegation (fixture backend skips) | `TestParseMutationContextMemberRefusals` |\n272|| N-body-scope | Body scope map (admits create) | `TestParseOperationBodyScopeGate` |\n273|| N-body-members | Body member set (admits one extra) | `TestParseOperationBodyRefusals` |\n274|| N-store-sweep-age | Sweep age gate (sweeps live-suffixed young staging) | `TestStoreSweepKeepsLiveStaging` |\n275|| N-result-effects-sort | Effects wire order (inverted) | `TestBuildResultSortsEffectsAndEvidence` |\n276|| N-result-evidence-sort | Evidence wire order (inverted) | `TestBuildResultSortsEffectsAndEvidence` |\n277|| C-control | Comment-only control (SURVIVED) | `TestRequiresProviderObservation` |\n278|\n279|## Stated bounds\n280|\n281|- No `ax` command, no doctor result, no runtime capability claim: the\n282|  `Backend` interface is modeled; tmux/ConPTY/process control and the\n283|  provider process do not exist here.\n284|- Terminal Instance Binding 1.0.0 closed-object parsing: no parser\n285|  exists on trunk (`canonicaljson` explicitly rejects\n286|  `urn:ax:schema:terminal-instance-binding`); the generation bound is\n287|  enforced on the surfaces this leaf owns and cited landed for the\n288|  Provider Protocol 3 descriptor (`terminalbackend` checkGeneration\n289|  arms). Full Binding parsing belongs with the provisioning surface.\n290|- CLI Result 4 summary: no landed Result 4 body carries a raw\n291|  generation member (`internal/cliresult` carries none by grep), so\n292|  there is no surface to witness the bound on; consistent with §4.E\n293|  (generation is host-local, non-replicable).\n294|- Attach, restore, terminate-stale, manifest, probe: refused by the\n295|  engine and body scope gates. Restore/terminate-stale recovery and\n296|  terminal binding events belong to the story's final leaf.\n297|- Create is receipt-scoped: receipt, transition, target and headless\n298|  rules execute; the full create body (Binding, Entrypoint,\n299|  presentation transport) belongs to provisioning.\n300|- Credential-realm conditional: credential need is not modeled on the\n301|  engine path.\n302|- Protocol_version membership in the admitted probe list is enforced at\n303|  registry admission (landed), not re-derived per operation; the\n304|  operation gate enforces grammar plus major 1 through the landed\n305|  `CheckVersionTuple` arms.\n306|- The per-code disposition mapping is the leaf's contract where the\n307|  spec pins the vocabulary but not the mapping; every arm is pinned\n308|  literally and mutated. In particular a lease rotation after a\n309|  committed effect reports `after=unavailable` with\n310|  `new_authorization` (the lease names its own remedy even though the\n311|  caller likely needs a status read too); §4.C's only sentence about\n312|  `unavailable` pairs it with `status_first`, so this pairing is the\n313|  leaf's stated contract, recorded as a literal tension, not a defect.\n314|- `holder_host_id` is parsed (UUIDv7) and never bound:\n315|  `CheckAuthorization` compares the §5.3 winning (lease_id, epoch)\n316|  tuple only, so a foreign holder under the winning tuple is\n317|  admitted. No path mints authority from the holder member.\n318|- Resumption re-issues effects under the SAME idempotency key and\n319|  relies on the backend's own key binding for safety (§4.C: \"AX and\n320|  backend durably bind the pair before the first child side effect\";\n321|  §13.13 safe_retry): the engine never issues one logical operation\n322|  under a second key, so no second process is allocated. For\n323|  wait-safe-boundary the source is the target, so a proven quiescing\n324|  resumes and the resumed observation supersedes any lost one; at\n325|  most one completion exists per key either way (no-replace).\n326|- A same-key retry that reconciles to the proven TARGET (or closed)\n327|  refuses uncertain rather than replaying: the effects may have\n328|  committed but their evidence cannot be proven, and re-issuing from\n329|  a non-source observation would violate the transition matrix. The\n330|  row recovery columns (\"then same-key retry only if not closed\")\n331|  are implemented as proceed-iff-source-proven.\n332|- AX-side seam emissions are outside the §4.C row sets: the row sets\n333|  govern backend reports (gated through the landed\n334|  `CheckErrorAllowed`), while an uncoded effect outcome classifies\n335|  `terminal_backend_process_failed` and an uncertain retry refuses\n336|  `terminal_backend_unavailable`, both with after `unavailable` and\n337|  `status_first` per the row recovery columns. Engine deadline\n338|  cancels before any attempt report `replay_same` on every row\n339|  (nothing was attempted); a backend-reported `stop_timeout` maps\n340|  through `DispositionFor` (`status_first` even uncommitted) because\n341|  the graceful wait ran. The two stop directions are pinned together\n342|  (`TestExecuteEntryDeadlineCodes`,\n343|  `TestExecuteBackendRowErrorSets`).\n344|- The wait/stop \"lesser of request deadline and timeout\" bound is\n345|  enforced by the backend wait (modeled here), which reports a coded\n346|  `quiesce_timeout`/`stop_timeout` proving non-commit; the engine\n347|  validates the timeout members (`uint53[1..3600000]`, carried in\n348|  `Params`) and enforces the `MutationContext` deadline.\n349|- Document member arms delegate their grammars to the landed\n350|  `environ`/`scalar` owners and are pinned literally through the\n351|  parse entries; where a Go-level twin re-validates with the same\n352|  detail, the Go twin carries the narrowing row (a document-side\n353|  weakening alone is masked by the twin). The body scope gate and\n354|  the body member-set gate have no twin and carry their own rows\n355|  (`N-body-scope`, `N-body-members`). The engine scope gate is\n356|  fail-fast ordering: admitting an operation past it is masked by\n357|  the `checkParams`/`KeySegments` scope defaults firing the same\n358|  detail (defense in depth, stated); `kindFor` is not redundant and\n359|  carries `N-engine-kind-map`.\n360|- The fencing operation must be launch-class (`restore`, equivalent\n361|  to `activation` on the stale arms and chosen for the terminal\n362|  domain); the non-launch entries refuse stale tokens instead of\n363|  parking them, measured by `N-fencing-operation` on the direct\n364|  question and `N-fencing-operation-remote` on the relative question.\n365|  The relative question re-authorizes from the winner's own host; it\n366|  composes the landed gate (no local tuple comparison) and fences\n367|  only on the relative stale verdict from a live source.\n368|- `internal/traceability` untouched per the Story contract; the final\n369|  leaf carries the registry bindings and the re-pin.\n370|\n371|## Inherited advisories (predecessor P3, for the record)\n372|\n373|- P3-6 closed by this leaf: the `Decision.Descriptor` doc in\n374|  `internal/axpane/decide.go` now states the recorded Binding\n375|  terminal instance ID is authoritative on reattach; this package's\n376|  `doc.go` states the consumer side.\n377|- P3-2 bound stated: this leaf adds no I/O-free `Decide` caller (the\n378|  engine never calls `Decide`), so the missing-closure input shape is\n379|  unreachable from this package; the pure-core hardening stays with\n380|  the owner.\n381|- P3-3 bound stated: this leaf never loads checkpoints (no\n382|  `LoadCheckpoint` caller), so the absent-store shape is unreachable\n383|  from this package.\n384|- P3-1, P3-4, P3-5 left to the final leaf (TASK-260830-2056mm):\n385|  journal-only restore closure (recovery domain), `EmitParked`\n386|  winner binding (events domain) and the corrupt-blob negative\n387|  (recovery domain) belong to events-and-recovery work.","final_result":true}}}
