{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c8a1","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b2ff-60d1-7b92-bcfc-8a4c766633f3"},"sequence":683,"recorded_at":1780531400001361,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"b5be48e9-caa3-42a3-a29a-786d769c2b71","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"b5be48e9-caa3-42a3-a29a-786d769c2b71","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"b5be48e9-caa3-42a3-a29a-786d769c2b71"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b301-259d-79c1-838f-bfa414392331"},"task_id":"01a0b301-259d-79c1-838f-bfa414392331","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b301-259d-79c1-838f-bfa414392331","chunk":"Read text file `internal/terminstance/doc.go`.\n1|// Package terminstance executes the Terminal Instance lifecycle contract of\n2|// SPEC §4.C over the landed internal/terminalbackend semantic core.\n3|//\n4|// Normative scope is relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec §4.C (lifecycle\n5|// state machine, transition/authorization/idempotency table), §4.B (the\n6|// backend_generation canonical bound), §4.D (capability conditionals\n7|// evaluated at the operation call site), §5.2 (status/unknown discipline),\n8|// §7.A (descriptor generation binding, cited landed) and §13.1 (durable\n9|// terminal entry before provider launch). Worked against\n10|// internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md: §§4.B, 4.C, 4.D, 5.2 and 7.A are\n11|// byte-identical to v0.6.0, while §13.1 carries the v0.7.0 launch-plan\n12|// insertion that precedes step 2 (a pure addition; the durable\n13|// terminal-entry rule text is unchanged).\n14|//\n15|// Composition, not re-implementation: the eight-state enum, the ten-operation\n16|// enum, the ten-effect enum, the transition matrix, the allowed-error sets,\n17|// the idempotency key shapes and the capability registry stay owned by\n18|// internal/terminalbackend (ParseInstanceState, ParseOperation,\n19|// ParseSideEffect, CheckTransition, CheckErrorAllowed, IdempotencyKey,\n20|// CheckOperation, GenerationDigest, CheckProviderDescriptor). Closed-shape\n21|// JSON admission stays owned by internal/environ (DecodeStrictObject,\n22|// CheckStringBounds, CheckUint53Bounds, CheckDigest, CheckUUIDv7,\n23|// CheckTimestamp, CheckSemver). Scalar grammars stay owned by\n24|// internal/scalar. Fencing truth stays owned by internal/fencing\n25|// (Authorize): this package never compares lease tuples itself to decide\n26|// staleness; ObserveFencing reads only the landed park vocabulary. What\n27|// this package owns is the execution layer the landed core deliberately\n28|// leaves out: the AXAuthorization closed object, the RetryDisposition and\n29|// ProviderProofKind closed enums, the mutating-request/response identity\n30|// contract, the per-side-effect recheck loop, the error-to-observation\n31|// mapping, and the durable idempotency receipt store.\n32|//\n33|// Stated bounds (no unsupported claims): no ax command, no tmux/ConPTY\n34|// process control and no provider process exist here; Backend is a modeled\n35|// caller interface. The Terminal Instance Binding 1.0.0 closed object has\n36|// no parser on trunk (canonicaljson explicitly rejects\n37|// urn:ax:schema:terminal-instance-binding) and the CLI Result 4 bodies\n38|// carry no raw generation member, so the generation bound is enforced on\n39|// the surfaces this leaf owns (operation bodies and results) and cited\n40|// landed for the Provider Protocol 3 descriptor; full Binding-object\n41|// parsing belongs with the provisioning surface. Attach, restore,\n42|// terminate-stale, manifest and probe operations are refused by the engine\n43|// scope gate; restore/terminate-stale recovery belongs to the story's\n44|// final leaf. Events (terminal.created/session.resumed emission) belong to\n45|// the final leaf. On reattach the recorded Binding terminal instance ID is\n46|// authoritative; a request-built descriptor names the request's own fresh\n47|// instance, never the recorded child.\n48|package terminstance","final_result":true}}}
