32, exit 1, no board-visible delta beyond the rev2\n22|tree). All rev2 production code, tests, and harness rows were kept;\n23|the changes below are the only delta.\n24|\n25|## Finding-by-finding table\n26|\n27|| Finding | Change (production call site) | Test that fails without it | Evidence path |\n28|| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n29|| F1: uncertain key poisoned forever; \"status, then same-key retry\" unimplementable | `Engine.resumeUncertain` (`execute.go`): a bound key without completion reconciles through the production `ExecuteStatus` with the exact-instance query; source-proven resumes under the same receipt via the shared `runEffects` loop (no second `Bind`); target/contradiction/unknown refuses `terminal_backend_unavailable`/`status_first`. `StoreHooks` doc reworded to reconcile-instead-of-replay | `TestExecuteUncertainRetryResumesWhenStatusProvesSource`, `TestExecuteRequestStopResumesWhenNotClosed`, `TestExecuteCreateResumesWhenStatusProvesAbsent` (each fails pre-fix: the post-status retry refused); `TestExecuteHookErrorRetryReconcilesThroughStatus/retry_resumes_on_proven_source` | `terminstance-test-v.log`, `mutants/pass{1,2}/N-resume-*.log` (6 rows) |\n30|| F1 crash extension | Same path, real kill | `TestExecuteCrashChildSelfTerminates` (extended: kill → uncertain refusal → status → same-key resume, one effect/result/receipt) and new `TestExecuteCrashCreateResumesAfterStatus` (kill → absent proof → identical create completes, one instance) | `terminstance-test-v.log` |\n31|| F2: stale incarnation under remote winner never fenced | `ObserveFencing` + `observeRemoteWinner` (`fencing.go`): on a `remote_owner` park, re-authorize from the winner's own host through the landed `fencing.Authorize` and fence only on the relative `stale_owner` verdict. No local tuple comparison | `TestObserveFencingRemoteWinnerStaleEpochFences`, `TestObserveFencingRemoteWinnerLosingLeaseFences` (fail pre-fix: no transition); `TestObserveFencingRemoteWinnerWinningTokenLeavesState` pins the no-transition member | `terminstance-test-v.log`, `mutants/pass{1,2}/N-fencing-remote*.log`, `N-fencing-operation-remote.log` |\n32|| E1: create row gates unmeasured at engine | No production change (gates existed); 4 committed tests + re-keyed rows | `TestExecuteCreateEntryAuthorizationRefuses` (3 subtests, no receipt bound), `TestExecuteCreateEntryGenerationRefuses` (no receipt), `TestExecuteCreateHeadlessFromAbsentNeedsCapability` (no receipt), `TestExecuteCreateCommittedTimeoutReportsStatusFirst` — each fails under its create-exempting mutant | `mutants/pass{1,2}/N-engine-{auth,generation}-entry.log` (re-keyed to create-exempt), `N-engine-headless-absent.log`, `N-engine-committed-timeout-disposition.log`; quiesce side kept as `N-engine-*-entry-quiesce` |\n33|| E2: recheck at one position; session never compared | No production change (loop + conjunction existed); rotation/drift tests at every position | `TestExecuteRechecksBeforeThirdEffect` (2 subtests), `TestExecuteStatusSessionDriftRefuses` (4 subtests: both lookup paths + sound non-match directions), `TestExecuteStatusIdentityMatchEachAxis` (10 subtests: 5 axes × admit/refuse) | `mutants/pass{1,2}/N-engine-recheck-*-third.log`, `N-status-session-*.log`, `N-status-match-*.log` (7 rows) |\n34|| P3-1: pre-link failure fences unavailable | `ExecuteMutating` Bind-error arm (`execute.go`): uncoded store failure + `Lookup` decides durability — nothing linked restores source, standing receipt / unreadable store fences uncertain | `TestExecutePreLinkStoreFailureRestoresSource` (fails pre-fix: after=unavailable), `TestExecuteStoreLookupFailureIsUncertain`, `TestExecuteHookErrorRetryReconcilesThroughStatus/standing_receipt_is_uncertain` | `mutants/pass{1,2}/N-engine-bind-prelink.log`, `N-engine-bind-postlink.log` |\n35|| P3-2: fencing sources unbounded | `fenceLive` (`fencing.go`): fence from creating/parked/active/quiescing; absent/stopped/stale_fenced/unavailable surface the park with no transition | `TestObserveFencingNonLiveSourcesLeaveState` (fails pre-fix on absent/stopped/unavailable) | `mutants/pass{1,2}/N-fencing-source-{absent,stopped,creating}.log` |\n36|| P3-3: deadline instant untested | No production change (`!Before` already refuses the instant); instant tests | `TestExecuteEntryDeadlineInstantRefuses` (4 rows), `TestExecuteStatusDeadlineInstantRefuses` | `mutants/pass{1,2}/N-engine-deadline-instant.log`, `N-status-deadline-instant.log` |\n37|| P3-4: `attach` admitted under narrowing | No production change (single `ParseAuthorizationKind` arm); corpus + rows | `TestParseAuthorizationKindClosed`, `TestParseAXAuthorizationKindClosed` (both extended with `attach`, `none`) | `mutants/pass{1,2}/N-auth-kind-{attach,none}.log` |\n38|| P3-5: match conjunction on generation axis only | No production change; per-axis tests | `TestExecuteStatusIdentityMatchEachAxis` (above; reviewer's probe committed in-style) | `N-status-match-*.log` (5 rows, one conjunct each) |\n39|| P3-6: `kindFor` restates landed column | New landed `terminalbackend.TransitionAuthorization` accessor (`conformance.go`); `kindFor` delegates to it (no restated table). Accessor registered in the backend's census/inventory/audit batteries | `TestTransitionAuthorizationReportsEveryTableColumn` (`terminalbackend`, 10 ops + unknown), `TestKindForAgreesWithLandedTable` (fails on drift either direction) | `cmd/cmd04.log` (terminalbackend suite), `mutants/pass{1,2}/N-engine-kind-map.log` (re-keyed) |\n40|| P3-7: `unavailable` + `new_authorization` | Judged: kept as the leaf's stated per-code contract (lease names its own remedy), recorded as a literal tension in TRACEABILITY bounds; no code change | `TestExecuteRechecksBeforeEachEffect/lease_rotates_mid-operation` (existing pin) | TRACEABILITY.md stated bounds |\n41|| `holder_host_id` unbound | Judged: stated bound in `CheckAuthorization` doc + TRACEABILITY (reviewer-confirmed non-violation); no code change | — (bound, not behavior) | `auth.go` doc, TRACEABILITY.md stated bounds |\n42|| TRACEABILITY 70/71 + \"recovers through status\" prose | Reworded to the resumed behavior (retry reconciles; refuses only while unknown); LOGBOOK rev2-F2 corrected by an explicit REVERSAL entry (additive, newest-first) | Rows 70–71 cite the extended crash tests | TRACEABILITY.md, LOGBOOK.md |\n43|\n44|Reviewer-mutant mirrors: all eleven rev2 reviewer narrowings\n45|(RV2-M1–M10, M15) are mirrored as committed harness rows with committed\n46|killers (`N-engine-recheck-{auth,generation}-third`,\n47|`N-engine-deadline-instant`, `N-status-deadline-instant`,\n48|`N-engine-committed-timeout-disposition`, `N-auth-kind-attach`,\n49|`N-engine-{auth,generation}-entry` re-keyed create-exempt,\n50|`N-status-match-implementation`, `N-engine-headless-absent`,\n51|`N-status-session-scoped`); the three reviewer controls map to the\n52|existing `N-auth-epoch-low` kill, build-break ERROR detection, and the\n53|`C-control` SURVIVED control.\n54|\n55|## AC coverage: 84 of 84 rows driven\n56|\n57|Measured, not restated: 84 data rows counted in\n58|`internal/terminstance/TRACEABILITY.md` (rows 1–72 keep rev2 numbers\n59|with 70/71 reworded; rows 73–84 are the rework rows), 98 cited\n60|top-level tests all present via `go test -list` (97 in-package + the\n61|`terminalbackend` column test), every cited subtest `--- PASS`, zero\n62|missing (see `ratio-check.log`); the full package suite is green\n63|(`terminstance-test-v.log`: exit 0, 101 `--- PASS`, 0 `--- FAIL` —\n64|the 4 in-package tests not cited in the matrix are supporting\n65|positive/store-level pins). Production call sites are named per row in\n66|the matrix and per clause in TRACEABILITY.md.\n67|\n68|## Negative and mutant evidence\n69|\n70|- `mutant_harness.py`: 100/100 rows match on two full passes with\n71|  identical verdict lists — 98 narrowing KILLED + 1 tightening edge\n72|  KILLED + the SURVIVED control. The tightening row\n73|  (`N-auth-epoch-high`) is unchanged and documented. Per-plant raw\n74|  logs with subprocess exits in `mutants/pass1/` and `mutants/pass2/`\n75|  (100 plants each, `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, no `__pycache__`);\n76|  production blobs verified byte-identical\n77|  before/after/across passes (`blob-*.txt`).\n78|- Crash/idempotency: no-replace link commits on receipt and completion\n79|  paths, `AfterCommit` hook seam, real-SIGKILL tests on BOTH the\n80|  quiesce seam (`TestExecuteCrashChildSelfTerminates`, extended) and\n81|  the create seam (`TestExecuteCrashCreateResumesAfterStatus`, new):\n82|  kill → receipt durable without completion → uncertain retry refuses\n83|  → status proves the source → same-key retry completes with exactly\n84|  one result and one receipt. A same-key retry without a status proof\n85|  still refuses.\n86|- No token-preserving source-text mutant applies: no gate inspects\n87|  source text.\n88|\n89|## Validation suite (configured commands, in order)\n90|\n91|Every command below is quoted from `task-board.config.json`\n92|`spawn.worktree_isolation.validation.commands` (30 commands) and was\n93|executed once against the exact candidate tree; logs in `cmd/`.\n94|Command 5 ran as 10 bounded chunks with identical flags (sessquery in\n95|3 `-run` shards; every other package whole; each package exactly\n96|once, no flags shortened) because a single shell call is\n97|time-bounded; see `cmd05-summary.txt` and `cmd05-r1..r10.log`.\n98|\n99|| # | Command | Exit |\n100|| --- | --- | --- |\n101|| 1 | `test -z \"$(gofmt -l $(git ls-files --cached --others --exclude-standard -- '*.go'))\"` | 0 |\n102|| 2 | `go build ./...` | 0 |\n103|| 3 | `go vet ./...` | 0 |\n104|| 4 | `go test ./... -count=1 -v` | 0 (40/40 packages ok) |\n105|| 5 | `go test ./... -race -count=1 -timeout 25m` | 0 (10 chunks, 40/40, 0 DATA RACE) |\n106|| 6 | `go test ./... -cover -count=1` | 0 (40/40; terminstance 85.6%) |\n107|| 7–10 | rpcwire fuzz ×4 (`-fuzztime=100x`) | 0 ×4 |\n108|| 11 | scalar fuzz ×1 | 0 |\n109|| 12–15 | canonicaljson fuzz ×4 | 0 ×4 |\n110|| 16–23 | secconftest fuzz ×8 | 0 ×8 |\n111|| 24 | `go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck` | 0 (contracts=64, cases=140, clauses 56/569 — trunk figures unchanged) |\n112|| 25 | `go run ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -adopted -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check` | 0, tree unmodified |\n113|| 26 | `GOOS=linux GOARCH=amd64 go build ./...` | 0 |\n114|| 27 | `GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go build ./...` | 0 |\n115|| 28 | `git ls-files -z '*.json' \\| xargs -0 -n1 python3 -c 'import json,sys;json.load(open(sys.argv[1]))'` | 0 |\n116|| 29 | `task-board validate` | 0 (zero issues name this task or story) |\n117|| 30 | `git diff --check` | 0 |\n118|\n119|An extra `GOOS=windows go vet` of the touched package also exits 0\n120|(`cmd27b-windows-vet.log`; not a configured command). The `.go` tree\n121|was verified byte-identical before and after the race gate\n122|(`go-sha-before-race.txt` == `go-sha-after-race.txt`), so the race\n123|ran against the exact candidate.\n124|\n125|## Files changed (rev3 delta on top of the rev2 tree)\n126|\n127|- `internal/terminstance/execute.go`: `resumeUncertain` +\n128|  `runEffects` extraction, pre/post-link `Bind` distinction,\n129|  `kindFor` delegation to the landed column.\n130|- `internal/terminstance/fencing.go`: relative-to-winner second\n131|  question (`observeRemoteWinner`), live-source gate (`fenceLive`).\n132|- `internal/terminstance/store.go`, `auth.go`: doc-only\n133|  (`StoreHooks` reconcile wording, `holder_host_id` bound).\n134|- `internal/terminstance/`: new `resume_test.go`,\n135|  `fencing_remote_test.go`, `create_gates_test.go`,\n136|  `recheck_test.go`; extended `crash_unix_test.go`,\n137|  `auth_test.go`, `disposition_test.go`; `mutant_harness.py`\n138|  70 → 100 rows; `TRACEABILITY.md` 72 → 84 rows.\n139|- `internal/terminalbackend/conformance.go`: new exported\n140|  `TransitionAuthorization` accessor; `conformance_test.go`,\n141|  `backend_id_entry_census_test.go`,\n142|  `refusal_arm_inventory_test.go`: column test + census/inventory/\n143|  audit registration (the unreachable-vocabulary bound now covers\n144|  both arms).\n145|- `README.md`: engine paragraph extended (remote fencing,\n146|  resumption), battery count 68 → 98 narrowing rows.\n147|- `LOGBOOK.md`: rev3 rework entry (additive, newest-first) with the\n148|  explicit rev2-F2 REVERSAL.\n149|- `internal/traceability` untouched per the Story contract.\n150|\n151|## Stated bounds (no unsupported claims)\n152|\n153|No `ax` command, doctor result, or runtime capability is added.\n154|Binding-object parsing, CLI Result 4, attach/restore/terminate-stale\n155|operations, full create body, credential conditionals, lesser-of\n156|timeout enforcement, and terminal events remain stated bounds (see\n157|TRACEABILITY.md). Newly stated: re-issue under the same key relies on\n158|the backend's key binding (§13.13); wait resumption supersedes (source\n159|is target, one completion per key); target-proven retries refuse\n160|uncertain (evidence unprovable); `holder_host_id` unbound;\n161|`unavailable`+`new_authorization` is the leaf's mapping contract. The\n162|per-code disposition mapping and the AX-side seam emission codes\n163|remain the leaf's contract where the spec pins the vocabulary but not\n164|the mapping.\n165|\n166|## Handoff\n167|\n168|Ready for review. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree;\n169|checklist updated on the board; outcome resources attached:\n170|`TASK-260830-kkh1an_results.md`,\n171|`TASK-260830-kkh1an_conformance-matrix.md`,\n172|`TASK-260830-kkh1an_producer-evidence.tar.gz`.","final_result":true}}}
