want KILLED) :: Decides exactly epoch-1 winnerless observations; other winnerless members stay undecided. [exit 1]\\nok: N-fencing-verdict-winner-shape: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Decides exactly epoch-1 malformed-winner observations; other malformed winners stay undecided. [exit 1]\\nok: N-fencing-verdict-session: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Decides exactly epoch-1 session-mismatched observations; other mismatches stay undecided. [exit 1]\\nok: N-fencing-verdict-handoff: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Decides exactly epoch-1 failed-handoff observations; the park is otherwise preserved. [exit 1]\\nok: N-fencing-verdict-presented-session: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Decides exactly the epoch-1 agreed-malformed session (both sides name one malformed session, so only the grammar arm undecides it); other malformed sessions still mismatch first. [exit 1]\\nok: N-fencing-verdict-presented-epoch: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Decides exactly the zero-epoch token under the losing test lease; the zero-epoch winning-lease member stays undecided. [exit 1]\\nok: N-fencing-verdict-presented-lease: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Decides exactly epoch-1 malformed-lease tokens; other malformed leases stay undecided. [exit 1]\\nok: N-fencing-verdict-composition: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Fences on decided alone instead of decided-stale: the winning token and the future epoch fence grant-less. (Dropping the decided conjunct instead would be equivalent — the verdict never reports stale undecided — so the decided half is measured by the eleven verdict rows above.) [exit 1]\\nok: N-engine-recheck-auth-expiry: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Drops the per-effect authorization EXPIRY recheck (expiry evaluated at the entry instant) while the lease-tuple recheck stays per-effect; the spanned definition+use is one plant — either half alone breaks the build. Mirrors reviewer narrowing RV3-M1. [exit 1]\\nok: N-result-evidence-bound: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly 257 evidence IDs on the one shared helper both the result and the status surface route through (one site, both surfaces in the killer). Mirrors reviewer narrowing RV3-M2. [exit 1]\\nok: N-engine-conditional-disposition: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Reports exactly the capability-conditional arm as status_first instead of the class-mapped required_operator_action. Mirrors reviewer narrowing RV3-M3. [exit 1]\\nok: N-proof-sibling: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly the landed capability name provider_process_observation as a proof kind; every other non-kind still refuses. Mirrors reviewer narrowing RV3-M4. [exit 1]\\nok: N-status-last-operation-empty: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly the empty last_operation_id on status reports; other non-UUIDv7 values still refuse. Mirrors reviewer narrowing RV3-M8. [exit 1]\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 3427,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 857,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
