{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d4d9","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b2ff-60d1-7b92-bcfc-8a4c766633f3"},"sequence":2247,"recorded_at":1780531400004489,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"b5be48e9-caa3-42a3-a29a-786d769c2b71","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"b5be48e9-caa3-42a3-a29a-786d769c2b71","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"b5be48e9-caa3-42a3-a29a-786d769c2b71"},"call_id":"call_01a0b30c65e7765090d6e4d63fc752b1","text":"Read text file `README.md`.\n(2214 line(s) above)\n2215|## Terminal Instance lifecycle execution (`terminstance` engine)\n2216|\n2217|[`internal/terminstance`](internal/terminstance) executes the Terminal\n2218|Instance lifecycle contract of the pinned Sections 4.B-4.D, 5.2, 7.A,\n2219|and 13.1 over the landed `terminalbackend` semantic core: the closed\n2220|`AXAuthorization` object (lease UUIDv4, epoch uint53 bound, holder\n2221|UUIDv7, kind, timestamps, evidence digest) parsed through the landed\n2222|`environ` closed-shape discipline, the closed `RetryDisposition` and\n2223|`ProviderProofKind` enums, the mutating-request/response identity\n2224|contract (`MutationContext`/`MutationResult` with exact idempotency key\n2225|material per row), and the `Engine` that binds the durable idempotency\n2226|receipt before the first side effect, rechecks authorization and\n2227|generation immediately before each side effect, restores the source\n2228|state on pre-effect errors, moves to `unavailable` with `status_first`\n2229|on unprovable post-effect errors (never claiming `absent`), and cancels\n2230|waiting — never a committed effect — on deadline. `creating` is entered\n2231|only by `create` between receipt and first effect, only `quiesce-input`\n2232|enters `quiescing`, and `stale_fenced` is entered only by fencing\n2233|observation through the landed `fencing` park vocabulary, never by a\n2234|backend operation — including under a remote winner, where staleness\n2235|is read relative to the winner from the winner's own host. A bound\n2236|key without its completion reconciles through the production status\n2237|entry: the same operation resumes under the same receipt when status\n2238|proves the source, and refuses uncertain otherwise. The receipt store\n2239|commits under the no-replace plus fsync discipline with crash hooks\n2240|and byte-agrees with the landed `Ledger` encoding; status performs no\n2241|receipt, effect, or transition of its own and a timeout or read\n2242|failure is unknown, never absent.\n2243|\n2244|Run the focused tests and coverage with:\n2245|\n2246|```bash\n2247|go test ./internal/terminstance -count=1\n2248|go test ./internal/terminstance -cover -count=1\n2249|```\n2250|\n2251|Run the narrowing battery (98 narrowing mutants, one tightening edge\n2252|row, plus one harmless control) with:\n2253|\n2254|```bash\n2255|PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/terminstance/mutant_harness.py\n2256|```\n2257|\n2258|The harness mutates one production file in place, runs the named killer\n2259|through the production entry point, restores the file from backup, and\n2260|reports per-row verdicts with subprocess exits; `AX_MUTANT_VERBOSE=1`\n2261|additionally prints the raw per-plant logs. Task validation logs and\n2262|mutation artifacts are attached to `TASK-260830-kkh1an`. The package\n2263|adds no `ax` command, no `doctor` result, and no runtime capability\n2264|claim; the clause-to-test matrix with its stated bounds lives in\n2265|[the task evidence map](internal/terminstance/TRACEABILITY.md).\n2266|\n2267|## Ownership reducer properties\n2268|\n2269|The four story-pinned ownership invariants (pinned v0.6.0 Sections 2.2, 5.3,\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
