{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d5c5","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b2ff-60d1-7b92-bcfc-8a4c766633f3"},"sequence":2365,"recorded_at":1780531400004725,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"b5be48e9-caa3-42a3-a29a-786d769c2b71","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"b5be48e9-caa3-42a3-a29a-786d769c2b71","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"b5be48e9-caa3-42a3-a29a-786d769c2b71"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b30c-dd7c-7b41-888a-e424f476d252"},"task_id":"01a0b30c-dd7c-7b41-888a-e424f476d252","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b30c-dd7c-7b41-888a-e424f476d252","chunk":"edited\nchanged lines: lines 6-8\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-## 2026-09-18\n-\n-### TASK-260830-kkh1an rev3 — Terminal Instance rework: resumption, remote fencing, row gates\n+## 2026-09-18\n+\n+### TASK-260830-kkh1an rev4 — Terminal Instance rework: grant-less fencing verdict, expiry recheck, P3 arms\n+- REWORKED after review-verdict-rev3 (no P1; P2 F3 production, P2 E3 evidence, 5 P3; the reviewer confirmed F1/F2/E1/E2 closed, the harness 100/100 twice, the 84/84 ratio, and a green suite — all kept untouched): F3 lands the exported `fencing.StaleRelativeToWinner` verdict (direction/tuple arms over a verified well-formed winner, no grant precondition — a grant authorizes, it never decides staleness) and composes it in `ObserveFencing` for grant-gated refusals, so the no-grant, lapsed-grant, no-clock and unusable-policy members fence from active/parked/quiescing under local and remote winners while unverified/ambiguous/winnerless/malformed/handoff-failed stay no-transition with the gate's own refusal or park; E3 commits the auth-expiry recheck witness (mid-operation expiry caught after one committed effect) plus a harness row that keeps the tuple recheck and drops the expiry recheck, and re-keys both E1 expired members onto the late-deadline instant so they kill on the receipt; P3-1..P3-4 commit the four reviewer witnesses with mirror rows, and P3-5 states the interim-proven create member with its `unavailable → terminate-stale` exit route.\n+- F1: the grant-precondition class is exactly four members (no grant, no clock reading, lapsed grant, unusable policy) because those are all four refusals `Authorize` can surface after the ownership arms pass — the verdict decides the tuple fact for all four uniformly by never consulting grant/clock/policy, so completeness is structural, not enumerated, and the relative question needs no fallback (same grant facts, and the grant arms do not read `LocalHostID`).\n+- F2: a narrowing row that spans a definition and its use is one plant, not two — the E3 row captures the entry instant and passes it to the in-loop authorization check, and either half alone breaks the build, so the kill measures the pair (same precedent as the rev3 resumption row spanning two adjacent checks).\n+- F3: a grammar arm masked by a downstream arm is unmeasurable alone — the verdict's presented-session grammar arm needed the agreed-malformed member (both sides naming one malformed session, so only the grammar arm undecides it) because any other malformed session mismatches first.\n+- MUTATION EVIDENCE: 115 narrowing mutants plus one tightening edge row, all KILLED (`mutant_harness.py`, 117/117 with the harmless SURVIVED control on two full passes, verdict lists identical), per-plant raw logs with subprocess exits on both passes, production blobs byte-identical before/after/across. The eleven verdict rows mutate the landed package and are killed through `ObserveFencing`, so the composition — not the helper — is measured. The seven rev3 reviewer narrowings are mirrored as committed rows with committed killers. No token-preserving source-text mutant applies: no gate inspects source text.\n+- AC: 93 of 93 rows driven through production entries by named tests (rows 1–84 keep rev3 numbers; rows 85–93 are the rework rows; matrix in `internal/terminstance/TRACEABILITY.md`); crash/idempotency evidence carried from rev3 (no new durable write — the verdict and the recheck are pure over their inputs). Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree; no review acceptance or main integration claimed.\n+\n+### TASK-260830-kkh1an rev3 — Terminal Instance rework: resumption, remote fencing, row gates\n","final_result":true}}}
