{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000dcb1","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b2ff-60d1-7b92-bcfc-8a4c766633f3"},"sequence":3251,"recorded_at":1780531400006497,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"b5be48e9-caa3-42a3-a29a-786d769c2b71","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"b5be48e9-caa3-42a3-a29a-786d769c2b71","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"b5be48e9-caa3-42a3-a29a-786d769c2b71"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b321-0f8a-7572-b212-00f78832dca3"},"task_id":"01a0b321-0f8a-7572-b212-00f78832dca3","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b321-0f8a-7572-b212-00f78832dca3","chunk":"Read text file `internal/terminstance/fencing.go`.\n(54 line(s) above)\n55|// unavailable (the observation is unknown and no verdict is projected\n56|// over unknown) surface the refusal with no transition. Every other\n57|// outcome leaves the state untouched: an authorized token reports no\n58|// transition, and any refusal or park the verdict cannot decide\n59|// (malformed, session mismatch, no winner, malformed winner,\n60|// unverified, ambiguous, failed handoff) or decides not-stale\n61|// (winning tuple, future epoch) surfaces its own error with no\n62|// transition, because only proven staleness fences. A nil error with\n63|// transitioned false is the authorized case.\n64|//\n65|// This function performs no lease comparison of its own: the tuple,\n66|// grant, expiry and direction arms all run inside the landed Authorize\n67|// and the landed StaleRelativeToWinner, so no second fencing model\n68|// exists here. It reads Winner.LeaseID and Winner.Epoch only through\n69|// those landed verdicts, never Winner.Checkpoint: lease records are\n70|// immutable content-addressed blobs whose checkpoint member is null\n71|// for every epoch-1 lease, so keying on it would be vacuous for every\n72|// session that never changed hands.\n73|func ObserveFencing(current terminalbackend.InstanceState, presented fencing.PresentedToken, observation fencing.Observation) (terminalbackend.InstanceState, bool, error) {\n74|\tif _, err := terminalbackend.ParseInstanceState(string(current)); err != nil {\n75|\t\treturn current, false, wrapLanded(err)\n76|\t}\n77|\t_, authErr := fencing.Authorize(fencing.OperationRestore, presented, observation)\n78|\tif authErr == nil {\n79|\t\treturn current, false, nil\n80|\t}\n81|\treason, _, parked := fencing.ParkDetails(authErr)\n82|\tif parked && reason == fencing.ParkRemoteOwner {\n83|\t\treturn observeRemoteWinner(current, presented, observation, authErr)\n84|\t}\n85|\tif parked && reason == fencing.ParkStaleOwner {\n86|\t\treturn fenceLive(current, authErr)\n87|\t}\n88|\tif stale, decided := fencing.StaleRelativeToWinner(presented, observation); decided && stale {\n89|\t\treturn fenceLive(current, authErr)\n90|\t}\n91|\treturn current, false, authErr\n92|}\n93|\n94|// observeRemoteWinner resolves a remote-winner park: the winner is on\n95|// another host and the presented token may be stale relative to it (the\n96|// force-takeover case) or the winning token itself observed from afar.\n97|// The landed gate decides from the winner's own host; only a stale\n98|// verdict fences, and only from a live incarnation.\n99|func observeRemoteWinner(current terminalbackend.InstanceState, presented fencing.PresentedToken, observation fencing.Observation, authErr error) (terminalbackend.InstanceState, bool, error) {\n100|\trelative := observation\n101|\trelative.LocalHostID = observation.Winner.HolderHostID\n102|\t_, relativeErr := fencing.Authorize(fencing.OperationRestore, presented, relative)\n103|\tif relativeErr == nil {\n104|\t\treturn current, false, authErr\n105|\t}\n106|\tif relativeReason, _, relativeParked := fencing.ParkDetails(relativeErr); relativeParked && relativeReason == fencing.ParkStaleOwner {\n107|\t\treturn fenceLive(current, authErr)\n108|\t}\n109|\treturn current, false, authErr\n110|}\n111|\n112|// fenceLive moves a live incarnation to stale_fenced and leaves every\n113|// other source untouched with the park that proved staleness. Absent\n114|// and stopped name no incarnation, stale_fenced is already fenced, and\n115|// unavailable is unknown: none of them transitions.\n116|func fenceLive(current terminalbackend.InstanceState, authErr error) (terminalbackend.InstanceState, bool, error) {\n117|\tswitch current {\n118|\tcase terminalbackend.StateCreating, terminalbackend.StateParked,\n119|\t\tterminalbackend.StateActive, terminalbackend.StateQuiescing:\n120|\t\treturn terminalbackend.StateStaleFenced, true, nil\n121|\tdefault:\n122|\t\treturn current, false, authErr\n123|\t}\n124|}","final_result":true}}}
