{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000e68f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b2ff-60d1-7b92-bcfc-8a4c766633f3"},"sequence":4514,"recorded_at":1780531400009023,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"b5be48e9-caa3-42a3-a29a-786d769c2b71","payload_type":"run.terminal.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"run_terminal","command_id":"b5be48e9-caa3-42a3-a29a-786d769c2b71","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"b5be48e9-caa3-42a3-a29a-786d769c2b71"},"terminal":"completed","text":"**Ready for review** — handed off to review (status `to-review`, checklist 19/19, three outcome resources attached).\n\n## What was done (rev4 rework of CR rev3, no P1)\n\n**F3 — grant-less stale members now fence.** Landed the reviewer-sanctioned exported verdict `fencing.StaleRelativeToWinner` ([staleness.go](/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-ptxkqe/worktree/internal/fencing/staleness.go)) — direction/tuple arms over a verified well-formed winner with no grant precondition — and composed it in `ObserveFencing` ([fencing.go](/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-ptxkqe/worktree/internal/terminstance/fencing.go:88)) for grant-gated refusals. The class is closed structurally, not by enumeration: the four grant-precondition refusals (no grant, no clock, lapsed, unusable policy) are all `Authorize` can surface after the ownership arms pass, and the verdict never consults grant/clock/policy. No-grant/lapsed/no-clock/unusable-policy × local/remote × epoch/mismatch × active/parked/quiescing all fence (48 transitions in `TestRV3F3_GrantLessStaleFences`, verified to fail 49 ways pre-fix); unverified/ambiguous/winnerless/malformed/handoff-failed/winning/future stay no-transition.\n\n**E3 — expiry axis pinned.** Committed `TestRV3W_M1_AuthExpiryRecheckedBeforeEachEffect` verbatim plus a harness row that keeps the per-effect tuple recheck and freezes only the expiry instant (spanned definition+use = one plant). Both E1 expired members re-keyed onto the late-deadline instant — all three create subtests now kill on the receipt.\n\n**P3** — all four witnesses committed verbatim with mirror rows; sibling vocabularies added to all three enum corpora; P3-5 interim-proven member stated with its `unavailable → terminate-stale` exit route.\n\n**Harness honesty:** the fallback made `N-fencing-epoch-only` provably equivalent (retired with proof) and `N-fencing-operation` needed re-keying to the non-live killer — both documented in TRACEABILITY, not hidden.\n\n## Evidence (all measured on the exact final tree)\n\n- 93/93 AC rows driven (109 top-level cited tests present and PASS)\n- Harness 116/116 on two passes, identical verdicts (114 narrowing KILLED + tightening + SURVIVED control), 232 per-plant raw logs with exits\n- Full 30-command suite green: 40/40 packages on `go test`, race (4 chunks), cover (terminstance 86.0%), 17 fuzz gates, tracecheck trunk figures, cataloggen, cross-builds, validate, diff-check\n- Real gzip evidence archive (286 entries, manifest-verified), no `__pycache__`, candidate left uncommitted on `c61fc06`, origin unchanged at `c3aae73`","reason":null}}
